hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21001","Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan ibn Harb ibn Umayyah ibn Abd Shams ibn Abd Manaf, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), her name was Ramlah, may Allah be pleased with her. Mention of the marriage of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Umm Habibah, from her reports. 401 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abil-Aswad, from Urwah ibn az-Zubayr, in the naming of those who emigrated to the land of Abyssinia with Jafar ibn Abi Talib, of Bani Asad ibn Khuzaymah: Ubaydullah ibn Jahsh ibn Riab, he died in the land of Abyssinia as a Christian, and with him was Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, and her name is Ramlah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) succeeded him upon her, Uthman ibn Affan married her to him in the land of Abyssinia, and Umm Habibah, her mother was Safiyyah bint Abi al-As, sister of Affan ibn Abi al-As, paternal aunt of Uthman ibn Affan."
"21002","402 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (Ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq at-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Yamar ibn Bashir narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from az-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn az-Zubayr, from Umm Habibah, that she was under Abdullah ibn Jahsh, and he traveled to an-Najashi and died, and that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Umm Habibah, while she was in the land of Abyssinia, an-Najashi married her to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not send anything to her, and the dowries of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were four hundred dirhams."
"21003","403 - Abu Usamah Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Usamah al-Halabi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Abi Mani narrated to us, from his grandfather Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad, from az-Zuhri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan ibn Harb ibn Umayyah ibn Abd Shams ibn Abd Manaf ibn Qusayy ibn Kilab ibn Murrah ibn Kab ibn Luayy ibn Ghalib ibn Fihr ibn Malik, and the name of Umm Habibah was Ramlah, and Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, married Umm Habibah, may Allah be pleased with her, to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), because Umm Habibah, her mother was Safiyyah bint Abi al-As, and Safiyyah was the paternal aunt of Uthman, full sister of Affan, and Shurahbil ibn Hasanah brought Umm Habibah to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"21004","404 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Abdil-Azim al-Anbari narrated to us, an-Nadr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abu Zumayl narrated to us, Ibn Abbas narrated to us, that Abu Sufyan said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): With me is the best and most beautiful of Arab women, Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, shall I marry her to you? He said: Yes. He said: And Muawiyah, you take him as a scribe? He said: Yes."
"21005","What Umm Habibah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), transmitted. What Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan narrated from his sister Umm Habibah. 405 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiyy narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abdil-Hakam narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Suwayd ibn Qays, from Muawiyah ibn Hudayj, he said: I heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan saying: I asked Umm Habibah, did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray in the garment in which he was intimate with her? She said: Yes, when there was no harm in it."
"21006","406 - Masadah ibn Sad al-Attar al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Suwayd ibn Qays, from Muawiyah ibn Hudayj, he said: I heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan saying: I asked Umm Habibah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray in the garment in which he was intimate? She said: Yes, when he did not see any harm in it."
"21007","407 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abdil-Jabbar ibn Umar narrated to us, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Yahya ibn Abi al-Muta, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, he said: I entered upon Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan and she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray in a single garment wrapped in it."
"21008","408 - Umar ibn Abdil-Aziz narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Suwayd ibn Qays, from Muawiyah ibn Hudayj, he said: I heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan saying: I asked Umm Habibah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray in the garment in which he was intimate with you? She said: Yes, when he did not see any harm in it."
"21009","What Anas ibn Malik narrated from Umm Habibah. 409 - Abu Zurah Abdur-Rahman ibn Amr ad-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abul-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah informed me, from az-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, from Umm Habibah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was shown what my ummah shall meet after me of some of them shedding the blood of others, so I asked Him to grant me intercession among them on the Day of Resurrection, so He did."
"21010","410 - Ahmad ibn Abdil-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Abul-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah informed us, from Abdullah ibn Abdir-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn, from Anas ibn Malik, from Umm Habibah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was shown what my ummah shall meet after me, and the shedding of its blood, so I asked Allah to grant me intercession among them, so He did."
"21011","411 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us, Sinan ibn Harun al-Burjumi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Umm Habibah said: O Messenger of Allah, a woman among us has two husbands then she dies and enters Paradise, she and her two husbands, for which of them shall she be, the first or the last? He said: She shall choose the best of them in character who was with her in the world, he shall be her husband in Paradise. O Umm Habibah, good character has taken the good of the world and the Hereafter."
"21012","Zaynab bint Abi Salamah from Umm Habibah. Urwah from Zaynab. 412 - Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, that Urwah ibn az-Zubayr narrated to him, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, that Umm Habibah said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Marry the daughter of Abu Sufyan to her sister. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you love that? She said: Yes, I am not alone with you, and the most beloved who shares with me in good is my sister. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is not lawful. Umm Habibah said: O Messenger of Allah, it is said that you are marrying Durrah bint Abi Salamah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The daughter of Umm Salamah? Umm Habibah said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If she were not my stepdaughter under my care, she would not be lawful, because she is the daughter of my brother through suckling, Thuwaybah suckled me, me and Abu Salamah, so do not offer to me your daughters nor your sisters."
"21013","413 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr at-Tustari narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Sad ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, my uncle Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Muslim, nephew of az-Zuhri, narrated to us, from his uncle Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Shihab, he said: Urwah ibn az-Zubayr informed me, that Zaynab bint Abi Salamah informed him, that Umm Habibah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed her, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, marry my sister, daughter of Abu Sufyan. She claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Do you love that? She said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, I am not alone with you, and the most beloved who shares with me in good is my sister. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is not lawful for me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are told that you intend to marry Durrah bint Abi Salamah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The daughter of Abu Salamah? She said: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, if she were not my stepdaughter under my care, she would not be lawful for me, because she is the daughter of my brother through suckling, Thuwaybah suckled me, and Abu Salamah, so do not offer to me your daughters, nor your sisters."
"21014","414 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ad-Dabari narrated to us, from Abdur-Razzaq, from Mamar, from az-Zuhri, Urwah ibn az-Zubayr said: From Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, that Umm Habibah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: O Messenger of Allah, marry my sister, daughter of Abu Sufyan. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Do you love that? She said: I am not alone with you, and the best who shares with me in good is my sister. He said: That is not lawful for me. She said: By Allah, we are told that you intend to marry Durrah bint Abi Salamah. He said: The daughter of Umm Salamah? She said: Yes. He said: By Allah, if she were not my stepdaughter, she would not be lawful for me, she is the daughter of my brother through suckling, Thuwaybah suckled me and her, so do not offer to me your daughters, nor your sisters."
"21015","415 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Ibn Aishah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Habibah, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, do you desire Hamnah bint Abi Sufyan? He said: Do what? She said: Marry her. He said: Is she lawful for me? She said: By Allah, I was informed that you are courting Zaynab bint Abi Salamah. He said: My stepdaughter under my care, by Allah if she were not my stepdaughter under my care, she is the daughter of my brother, Thuwaybah suckled me and her, so do not offer to me your daughters nor your sisters nor your mothers."
"21016","416 - Ali ibn Abdil-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, that Umm Habibah said: O Messenger of Allah, then he mentioned the like of it."
"21017","417 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak as-Sanani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Habibah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me, so I said: Do you desire my sister, daughter of Abi Sufyan? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do what? I said: Marry her. He said: Your sister? I said: Yes. He said: Do you love that? I said: Yes, I am not alone with you, and the most beloved who shares with me in good is my sister. He said: She is not lawful for me. I said: By Allah, I was informed that you are courting the daughter of Abi Salamah. He said: The daughter of Abi Salamah? I said: Yes. He said: By Allah, if she were not my stepdaughter under my care, she would not be lawful for me, she is the daughter of my brother through suckling, Thuwaybah suckled me and her, so do not offer to me your daughters and your sisters."
"21018","418 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ad-Dabari narrated to us, Abdur-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Mamar, they said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Urwah, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Habibah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me, so I said: Do you desire my sister, daughter of Abi Sufyan? He said: Do what? I said: Marry her. He said: Your sister? I said: Yes. He said: Do you love that? I said: Yes, I am not alone with you, and the most beloved, or she said, and the most deserving who shares with me in good is my sister. He said: She is not lawful for me. She said: By Allah, I was informed that you are courting Durrah bint Abi Salamah. He said: The daughter of Abi Salamah? I said: Yes. He said: By Allah, if she were not my stepdaughter under my care, she would not be lawful for me, she is the daughter of my brother through suckling, Thuwaybah suckled me and her, so do not offer to me your daughters nor your sisters."
"21019","Irak ibn Malik from Zaynab. 419 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Irak ibn Malik, that Zaynab bint Abi Salamah informed him, that Umm Habibah said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): We have been told that you are marrying Durrah bint Abi Salamah. So he said: My wife Umm Salamah? If I had not married Umm Salamah, she would not be lawful for me, her father is my brother through suckling."
"21020","Humayd ibn Nafi from Zaynab. 420 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ad-Dabari narrated to us, from Abdur-Razzaq, (Ha). And Ali ibn Abdil-Aziz narrated to us, and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, they said: al-Qanabi narrated to us, (Ha). And Bakr ibn Sahl ad-Dimyati narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, all of them from Malik ibn Anas, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Humayd ibn Nafi, that Zaynab bint Abi Salamah informed him, that she entered upon Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when her father Abu Sufyan died, so Umm Habibah called for perfume in which was yellowness, khaluq or other, so she anointed a slave-girl from it, then touched her cheeks, then said: By Allah, I have no need of perfume, except that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person more than three nights, except over a husband, four months and ten days."
"21021","421 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, he said: Humayd ibn Nafi narrated to me, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, that when the news of her father came, she called for perfume and wiped her arms with it, and said: By Allah, I have no need of perfume, were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person more than three nights, except over a husband, four months and ten days."
"21022","422 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Ayyub ibn Musa narrated to me, from Humayd ibn Nafi, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Habibah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person more than three nights, except over a husband, four months and ten days."
"21023","423 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar ar-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Humayd ibn Nafi, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Habibah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person more than three nights, except over a husband."
"21024","424 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, from Humayd ibn Nafi, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Habibah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person more than three, except over a husband."
"21025","425 - Ali ibn Abdil-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, (Ha). And Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Awn Abu Awn az-Ziyadi narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said informed us, from Humayd ibn Nafi, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, and Umm Habibah, that a woman said: O Messenger of Allah, my daughter, her husband has died, and I fear for her eyesight, shall I apply kohl to her? He said: One of you used to throw dung upon the head of the year, and it is only four months and ten days."
"21026","426 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Humayd ibn Nafi', from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, that a woman asked Umm Salamah and Umm Habibah: 'May a woman apply kohl during her waiting period after her husband's death?' They said: A woman came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and asked him about that, and he said: 'In the pre-Islamic period, when one's husband died, one of you would stay for a year, then throw a dung, but it is only four months and ten days until the term passes.'"
"21027","427 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Humayd ibn Nafi', that he heard Zaynab bint Abi Salamah saying: I heard Umm Salamah and Umm Habibah mention, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - the story of the waiting period."
"21028","Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Abi Sufyan from Umm Habibah. 428 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Abu Bishr, who said: I heard Abu al-Malih narrating from Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Umm Habibah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - when he heard the mu'adhdhin, would repeat what he said until he fell silent."
"21029","Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan from Umm Habibah. 430 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, (Ha). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, (Ha). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abidah ibn Humayd and Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, all of them from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Nu'man ibn Salim, from Amr ibn Aws, who said: I entered upon Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, who said: Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan narrated to me, from the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - who said: 'Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise.' Umm Habibah said: I have not abandoned them since I heard them from the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Amr said: I have not abandoned them since I heard them from Anbasah. And the wording is that of Amr ibn Awn."
"21030","431 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Nu'man ibn Salim, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: 'Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise.'"
"21031","432 - Abu Yazid Yusuf ibn Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Aws al-Thaqafi, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah - wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and she is his sister - that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Twelve rak'ahs: whoever prays them, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise: four rak'ahs before Zuhr, two rak'ahs after Zuhr, two rak'ahs before Asr, two rak'ahs after Maghrib, and two rak'ahs before Fajr.'"
"21032","433 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from Amr ibn Aws al-Thaqafi, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, from the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - who said: 'Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, Allah builds for him thereby a house in Paradise: four rak'ahs before Zuhr, two rak'ahs after Zuhr, two rak'ahs before Asr, two rak'ahs after Maghrib, and two rak'ahs before Fajr.'"
"21033","434 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Salim ibn Munqidh, from Amr ibn Aws al-Thaqafi, who said: I entered upon Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan while he was dying, and he said: I shall narrate to you a hadith which Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan narrated to me; she narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs along with the daytime prayer, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise.'"
"21034","435 - Muhammad ibn Jaban al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Allan al-Marwazi narrated to us, Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, who said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day and night, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise: four before Zuhr, two rak'ahs after it, two rak'ahs after Maghrib, two rak'ahs after Isha, and two rak'ahs before the morning prayer.'"
"21035","436 - Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, (Ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun and Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - who said: 'Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day and night apart from the obligatory prayer, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise.'"
"21036","437 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Aban, from Sulayman ibn Qays, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise, and whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise.'"
"21037","438 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Umar ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to me, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jafari, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, from the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - who said: 'Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise: four rak'ahs before Zuhr, two rak'ahs after Zuhr, two rak'ahs before Asr, two rak'ahs after Maghrib, and two rak'ahs after Isha.'"
"21038","439 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, who said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in his night and day apart from the obligatory prayer, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise.'"
"21039","440 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, (Ha). And Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, both said: Mufaddal ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: 'Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs apart from the obligatory prayer, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise.'"
"21040","441 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, al-Nu'man ibn al-Mundhir informed us, from Makhul, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, that she informed him that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Whoever regularly observes four rak'ahs before the midday prayer and four after it shall be made forbidden to Hell.'"
"21041","442 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from al-Nu'man ibn al-Mundhir, from Makhul, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, who informed him, from the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - that he said: 'Whoever regularly observes four rak'ahs before Zuhr and four after it, Allah makes him forbidden to the Fire.'"
"21042","443 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ya'ish narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated to us, from his father, from Makhul, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, from the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - who said: 'Whoever regularly observes four rak'ahs before the midday prayer and four after it shall be made forbidden to Hell.'"
"21043","444 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Isra'il ibn Yunus, from Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah ibn al-Muhajir, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, that she heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: 'Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr, Allah makes the Fire forbidden for him.'"
"21044","445 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah al-Shu'aythi narrated to us, from his father, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - who said: 'Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr and four after it, Allah makes him forbidden to the Fire.'"
"21045","446 - Salamah ibn Nahid al-Maqdisi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Hani ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah narrated to us, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, who said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr, Allah makes his body forbidden to the Fire.'"
"21046","447 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, al-Ala ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Makhul, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, that she heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: 'Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution.'"
"21047","448 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Ta'ifi, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, who said: Safwan ibn Ya'la ibn Umayyah narrated to me, who said: I came to Ta'if to visit Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan while he was dying and was distressed by that, so we said: Rejoice, O Abu Uthman, for we hope good for you. He said: My sister Umm Habibah - wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - narrated to me that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs by night or day apart from the obligatory prayer, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise.' I have not abandoned them since I heard them."
"21048","449 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Nu'man ibn Salim, from Amr ibn Aws, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, who said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day and night, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise.'"
"21049","450 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, Abu Mushir narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Harith, from Makhul, from Anbasah, from Umm Habibah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Whoever touches his male organ, let him perform ablution.'"
"21050","451 - Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Khalid narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muhammad narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Harith, from Makhul, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, who said: I heard the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: 'Whoever touches his male organ, let him perform ablution.'"
"21051","452 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Khalid narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Makhul, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - who said: 'Whoever performs four rak'ahs before Zuhr and four rak'ahs after it, Allah makes him forbidden to the Fire.'"
"21052","453 - Yahya ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, al-Ala ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: 'Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr and four after it, Allah makes him forbidden to the Fire.'"
"21053","454 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Hashim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Husayn, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from Dhakwan Abu Salih, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - who said: 'Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, a house is built for him in Paradise.'"
"21054","455 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - the same."
"21055","456 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Shaybani narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, who said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Makhul, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, who said: My sister Umm Habibah informed me that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr and four after it, Allah makes him forbidden to the Fire.'"
"21056","457 - Yahya ibn Uthman narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Makhul, from a freedman of Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, that the Prophet said: 'Whoever prays four before Zuhr and four after it, Allah makes him forbidden to the Fire.'"
"21057","458 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from al-Nu'man ibn al-Mundhir, from Makhul, from Anbasah, from Umm Habibah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - the same."
"21058","459 - Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Awf narrated to us, al-Rabi' ibn Rawh narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Basri, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Muhajir, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, who said: Umm Habibah narrated to me that she heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: 'Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr and four after it, Allah makes him forbidden to the Fire.'"
"21059","460 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan narrated to me, from Umm Habibah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: 'Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in his night and day, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise.'"
"21060","461 - Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Sufyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan narrated to us, Ma'mar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Zayd ibn Hibban narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: 'Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise.'"
"21061","Abu Sufyan ibn Sa'id ibn al-Mughirah ibn al-Akhnas from Umm Habibah. 462 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Sufyan ibn Sa'id ibn al-Akhnas, that he entered upon Umm Habibah and she gave him sawiq to drink, then he stood to pray, and she said to him: Perform ablution, O son of my brother, for I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: 'Perform ablution from what fire has touched.'"
"21062","463 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Sufyan ibn Sa'id ibn al-Akhnas, from Umm Habibah, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Perform ablution from what fire has touched.'"
"21063","464 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Imami informed us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Sufyan ibn Sa'id ibn al-Akhnas, from Umm Habibah, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Perform ablution from what fire has touched.'"
"21064","465 - Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah, from Bakr ibn Sawadah, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Sufyan ibn Sa'id ibn al-Akhnas, from Umm Habibah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: 'Ablution is from what fire has touched.'"
"21065","Abu Sufyan, son of Umm Habibah's sister. 466 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, that Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed him, that Abu Sufyan ibn Sa'id ibn al-Akhnas informed him, that he entered upon his maternal aunt Umm Habibah - wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and she stirred sawiq for him and he drank it, and she said: O my son, perform ablution, for I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: 'Ablution is from what fire has touched.'"
"21066","467 - Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Sufyan ibn Sa'id ibn al-Akhnas, from Umm Habibah, who said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Perform ablution from what fire has touched.'"
"21067","468 - Ahmad ibn al-Khattab al-Tustari narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Sa'd al-Zuhri narrated to us, who said: My uncle Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Sufyan ibn Sa'id ibn al-Akhnas, from Umm Habibah, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - commanded ablution from food that fire has touched."
"21068","469 - Abu Hanifah Muhammad ibn Hanifah al-Wasiti narrated to us, my uncle Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahan narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Ala ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Hakim, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Sufyan ibn Sa'id ibn al-Akhnas, from Umm Habibah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: 'Perform ablution from what fire has touched.'"
"21069","470 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, that Abu Sufyan ibn al-Mughirah narrated to him, that he entered upon Umm Habibah and she gave him a cup of sawiq to drink, then he called for water and rinsed his mouth, and she said to him: O son of my sister, will you not perform ablution, for the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Perform ablution from what fire has altered or touched.'"
"21070","al-Jarrah, also called Abu al-Jarrah, freedman of Umm Habibah, from Umm Habibah. 472 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from al-Jarrah, freedman of Umm Habibah, from Umm Habibah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: 'The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell.'"
"21071","473 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Nafi', from Salim, from al-Jarrah, freedman of Umm Habibah, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'A caravan in which there is a bell is not accompanied by the angels.'"
"21072","474 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Abi Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Salim, from al-Jarrah, freedman of Umm Habibah, who heard him informing Ibn Umar, from Umm Habibah, that she informed him that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'A caravan in which there is a bell is not accompanied by the angels.'"
"21073","475 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Salim, from Abu al-Jarrah, freedman of Umm Habibah, from Umm Habibah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - who said: 'The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell.'"
"21074","476 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abduh ibn Sulayman and Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Salim, from Abu al-Jarrah, freedman of Umm Habibah, from Umm Habibah, who said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell.'"
"21075","477 - Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mudrik al-Qasri narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu Khulayd Utbah ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, from Nafi', from Salim, from Abu al-Jarrah, freedman of Umm Habibah, from Umm Habibah, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'A caravan in which there is a bell is not accompanied by the angels.'"
"21076","478 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya, scribe of al-Umari, narrated to us, al-Mufaddal ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Sulayman al-Tawil, from Nafi', that Salim informed him, that Umm Habibah informed him, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell.'"
"21077","479 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah, from Irak ibn Malik, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from al-Jarrah, from Umm Habibah, that she heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: 'The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell.'"
"21078","Dhakwan Abu Salih al-Samman from Umm Habibah. 480 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Salih, from Umm Habibah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise.'"
"21079","Salim ibn Shawwal from Umm Habibah. 481 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, (Ha). And Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, who said: My father narrated to me, both said: Sufyan narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, who said: I heard Salim ibn Shawwal narrating from Umm Habibah, who said: We used to do it in the time of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - we would depart early from Muzdalifah to Mina. Al-Humaydi added in his hadith: Sufyan said: Salim ibn Shawwal is a man of the people of Makkah; we have not heard anyone narrate from him except Amr ibn Dinar, this hadith."
"21080","Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami from Umm Habibah. 482 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Umm Habibah, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - used to pray on a khumrah."
"21081","Amr ibn al-Hakam from Umm Habibah. 483 - Abd al-Malik ibn Yahya ibn Bukayr al-Misri narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Darraj Abu al-Samh, from Amr ibn al-Hakam, from Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, who said: Some people of Yemen came to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and he taught them the prayer, the practices, and the obligations, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, we have a drink we make from wheat and barley. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Do not make it.'"
"21082","Safiyyah bint Shaybah from Umm Habibah. 484 - Abu Harun Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Sirini narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Khunays al-Makki narrated to us, who said: We entered upon Sufyan al-Thawri visiting him in sickness, and Sa'id ibn Hassan al-Makhzumi entered upon him, and Sufyan said to him: Repeat to me the hadith of Umm Salih. He said: Umm Salih narrated to me, (Ha). And al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Mujashi'i narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Ya'qub al-Kirmani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Khunays al-Makki narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Hassan, who said: Umm Salih narrated to me, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Umm Habibah - wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - who said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'All the speech of the son of Adam is against him, not for him, except enjoining good, or forbidding evil, or remembrance of Allah.' A man among the people said: How severe is this hadith. Sufyan al-Thawri said: And what is its severity? Has not your Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - come to you from your Lord - Mighty and Majestic - saying: {The Day the Spirit and the angels will stand in rows; they will not speak except one whom the Most Merciful permits and who says what is right. That is the True Day} and saying: {No good is there in much of their private conversation except one who orders charity or good or reconciliation between people} to the end of the verse."
"21083","Umm Alqamah from Umm Habibah. 485 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn al-Taymi, from al-Salt, meaning Ibn Dinar, from Alqamah, from his mother, from Umm Habibah, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - was in her house and heard the mu'adhdhin, and he repeated what he said; when he said: Come to prayer, the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - rose to prayer."
"21084","486 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Rawasibi narrated to us, Fudalah ibn Husayn al-Attar narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Umm Habibah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - who said: 'Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day apart from the obligatory prayer, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise.'"
"21085","487 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Salim, from Abu al-Jarrah, from Umm Habibah, who said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell.'"
"21086","488 - Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Sufyan ibn Sa'id, from Umm Habibah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Perform ablution from what fire has touched.'"
"21087","489 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ansari narrated to us, al-Zuhri informed me, Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, who said: Abu Sufyan ibn Sa'id ibn al-Akhnas informed me, from Umm Habibah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - the same."
"21088","490 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Salim ibn Shawwal, from Umm Habibah, who said: We used to do it in the time of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - in the early darkness from Muzdalifah to Mina."
"21089","491 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, who said: Damrah ibn Habib narrated to me, who said: Muhammad ibn Abi Sufyan al-Thaqafi narrated to me, from Umm Habibah, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - in a garment upon me and upon him in which there was what there was."
"21090","492 - Hajjaj ibn Imran narrated to us, Yahya ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from Shutayr ibn Shakl, from Umm Habibah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - used to kiss while fasting."
"21091","493 - Yahya ibn Salih narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu al-Duha, from Shutayr ibn Shakl, from Umm Habibah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - used to kiss while fasting."
"21092","494 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from Atiyyah ibn Qays, that Umm Habibah was in the land of Abyssinia with Ja'far ibn Abi Talib, and that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - married her, and al-Najashi gave four hundred dinars as dowry on his behalf."
"21093","495 - Yahya ibn Uthman narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ghalib narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Darraj, from Umar ibn al-Hakam, from Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, that some people of Yemen came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and he taught them the practices, the prayer, and the obligations, and they said: We have a drink we make from wheat and barley. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Al-Ghubayra?' They said: Yes. He said: 'Then do not taste it.' They said: But they will not abandon it. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Whoever does not abandon it, strike his neck.'"
"21094","Umm Salamah, whose name is Hind bint Abi Umayyah ibn Hudhayfah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Makhzum ibn Nuqtah ibn Murrah ibn Ka'b ibn Lu'ayy ibn Ghalib. 496 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us with this lineage, who said: al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar narrated to us. Umm Salamah was, before the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - with Abu Salamah Abdullah ibn Abd al-Asad, and she bore him Salamah, Umar, and Zaynab, then he died leaving her, and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - married her after him."
"21095","497 - Mu'adh al-Halabi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Abdi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, who said: Umar ibn Abi Salamah informed me, from his mother Umm Salamah, from her husband Abu Salamah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: 'There is no Muslim afflicted with an affliction who says: To Allah we belong and to Him we return, O Allah, I seek the reward of my affliction with You, O Allah, replace it for me with better than it, except that Allah replaces it for him with better than it.' When Abu Salamah died, Umm Salamah said: To Allah we belong and to Him we return, O Allah, I seek the reward of my affliction in Abu Salamah with You, O Allah, replace him for me with better than him. I kept saying to myself: Who is better than Abu Salamah? Then the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - came and proposed to me, and I said: I am a woman with children, I am jealous, and I am advanced in age. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'As for advanced age, I am older than you; as for jealousy, I shall supplicate Allah to remove it from you; and as for dependents, they are to Allah and His Messenger.' Then he commanded Umar ibn Abi Salamah, who married me to him."
"21096","498 - Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, (Ha). And Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, both said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - married Umm Salamah for a trousseau worth ten dirhams."
"21097","499 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham narrated to us, who said: Umm Salamah said: When the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - proposed to me, I said to him: I have three traits in me: I am advanced in age, I am a woman with small children, and I am a very jealous woman. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'As for age, I am older than you; as for children, they are to Allah and His Messenger; and as for jealousy, I shall supplicate Allah to remove it from you.' So the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - married her, and when he came to her he said: 'You and your family have honor with me, and I have not given seven to any of my wives; if I give seven to you, I shall give seven to my wives.'"
"21098","500 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Madini Fustuqah narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, from al-Haytham ibn Adi, who said: The first of the Prophet's wives - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - to die was Zaynab bint Jahsh; she died during the caliphate of Umar, and the last of them to die was Umm Salamah; she died in the time of Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah in the year sixty-two."
"21099","What Umm Salamah narrated. A'ishah, Mother of the Believers, from Umm Salamah - may Allah be pleased with them both. 501 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from Dhakwan, from A'ishah, that Umm Salamah said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - came to me after Asr and prayed two rak'ahs, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, what are these two rak'ahs? He said: 'I used to pray them after Zuhr, then a situation came to me and distracted me from them until I prayed Asr, so I have prayed them now.'"
"21100","502 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, who said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sufyan ibn Huwaytib, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from A'ishah, who said: Umm Salamah narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - prayed them in her house."
"21101","Abu Sa'id al-Khudri from Umm Salamah. 503 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Atiyyah narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id, who said: Umm Salamah said: This verse was revealed in my house: {Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the House, and to purify you thoroughly}, while I was sitting at the door. I said: O Messenger of Allah, am I not of the people of the House? He said: 'You are toward good.'"
"21102","Umar ibn Abi Salamah from Umm Salamah. 504 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Duhaym narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr: 'Enter ihram for Hajj and say: My place of release is where You confine me.'"
"21103","505 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, (Ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated to us, both said: Abu Aqil Yahya ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Rafi' narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'If the first thing my Lord entrusted to me and forbade me after worship of idols and drinking wine was quarreling with men.'"
"21104","506 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, who said: Ibn Umar ibn Abi Salamah informed me, from his father, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to her when he married her: 'If you wish, I shall give you seven, then I shall give seven to the rest of my wives.'"
"21105","507 - And from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -: 'There is no one afflicted with an affliction...' and he mentioned the hadith."
"21106","Anas ibn Malik from Umm Salamah. 508 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (Ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, both said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: I was in Basra, and Anas ibn Malik said: Umm Salamah informed me that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'I have seen what my ummah will face after me, so I have delayed my intercession until the Day of Resurrection.'"
"21107","Buraydah ibn al-Husayb al-Aslami from Umm Salamah. 509 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Tumaylah Yahya ibn Wadih narrated to us, who said: Abdullah ibn Salim Abu Qutaybah informed me, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from his father, that Umm Salamah was in the expedition of Khaybar, and she said: 'I heard the clash of the sword on the teeth of Marhab.'"
"21108","510 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abu Tumaylah narrated to us, Abd al-Mu'min ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Gabriel has not ceased enjoining upon me the siwak until I feared for my molars.'"
"21109","Sulayman ibn Buraydah from Umm Salamah. 511 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, Ayyub al-Wazzan narrated to us, Fuhayr ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abu Shaybah narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from Umm Salamah, who said: O Messenger of Allah, is jihad upon women? He said: 'Their jihad is here,' and he gestured with his hand toward Makkah."
"21110","Abu Rafi' from Umm Salamah. 512 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mukhawwal ibn Rashid, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Rafi', from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - forbade a man to pray with his head tied in a knot."
"21111","Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Umm Salamah; Abu Ishaq from Abu Salamah. 513 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah, who said: By the One who took his soul - meaning the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - he did not die until most of his prayer was sitting except the obligatory prayer, and the most beloved deed to him was that which its doer persists in, even if it was little."
"21112","514 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, (Ha). And Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qitrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Tufayl narrated to us, both said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: The most beloved deeds to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - were those persisted in, even if little."
"21113","515 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abdullah al-Bakka'i narrated to us, Rahil ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: He did not die until most of his prayer was sitting, and the most beloved deed to him was that which its doer persists in, even if little - meaning the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"21114","516 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: By the One who took his soul, he did not die until most of his prayer was while sitting, and the most beloved deeds to him were the righteous deed which the servant persists in, even if it was little."
"21115","517 - Abu Yahya al-Dari narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Mu'ammal narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'A woman should not ask for the divorce of her sister to empty what is in her bowl, for her provision is only upon Allah - Mighty and Majestic.'"
"21116","518 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ma'mari, Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh, and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, who said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Ayshi narrated to us, Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, from Isra'il ibn Yunus, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - that he came to her, wrapped his cloak, placed it on the threshold of the door, leaned upon it, and said: 'Will you have me, O Umm Salamah?' She said: I am a very jealous woman, and I fear that there may appear to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - from me what he dislikes. So he left, then returned and said: 'Will you have me, O Umm Salamah? If it is an increase in your dowry you want, we shall increase.' She repeated her statement, then Umm Abd said: O Umm Salamah, do you know what the women of Quraysh are saying? They say that Umm Salamah only rejected Muhammad because she wanted a young man of Quraysh younger than him in age and richer in wealth. She said: Then she came to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and he married her."
"21117","Ammar al-Duhni from Abu Salamah from Umm Salamah. 519 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'The legs of my pulpit are fixed in Paradise.'"
"21118","520 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'The legs of my pulpit are fixed in Paradise.'"
"21119","521 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Abi Mu'awiyah, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: I used to bathe with the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - from a single vessel."
"21120","522 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, similar."
"21121","523 - Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Warah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - similar."
"21122","524 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Tamim ibn al-Muntasir narrated to us, Ishaq narrated to us, from Sharik, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - used to deliver the sermon leaning against a trunk in the mosque; when the pulpit was made, the trunk moaned, so the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - embraced it, and it fell silent."
"21123","525 - Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Warah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - the same."
"21124","526 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Between my house and my pulpit is a garden of the gardens of Paradise.'"
"21125","Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd from Abu Salamah from Umm Salamah. 527 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Shu'bah ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Mansur, who said: I heard Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd narrating from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would not fast a complete month, except that he would fast Sha'ban and join it to Ramadan."
"21126","528 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abu Salamah, from A'ishah and Umm Salamah, who both said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would not fast any month besides Ramadan except Sha'ban, for he would join it to Ramadan, making two consecutive months; he would fast the month until we said he will not break fast, and break fast until we said he will not fast."
"21127","529 - al-Husayn narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from his father, from Mansur, from Salim, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would fast Sha'ban and Ramadan."
"21128","530 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ali ibn Harb narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abi Hawdhah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Qays, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abu Salamah, similar."
"21129","Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay' from Abu Salamah from Umm Salamah. 531 - al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya Sa'iqah narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that a slave girl was married by her father while she wanted to marry another man, so she came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and mentioned that to him, and he took her away from the man whom her father had married her to, and the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - married her to the one she wanted."
"21130","532 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Rizqullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shababuh narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', who said: I heard Abu Salamah, that Umm Salamah asked the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - about a woman who has a wet dream, and he said: 'Does she find desire?' She said: Yes. He said: 'Then let her bathe.'"
"21131","Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Salamah from Umm Salamah. 533 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: I was with the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - in his quilt and I menstruated, so I slipped away from him, and he said: 'What is wrong with you, have you menstruated?' meaning menstruation. I said: Yes. She said: So I tightened my menstrual garments upon me, then returned and lay down with the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"21132","534 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah, who said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - pray after Asr at all except once: some people came to him after Zuhr and distracted him until he forgot, so he did not pray anything after Zuhr until he prayed Asr; when he prayed Asr, he entered my house and prayed two rak'ahs."
"21133","535 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abi al-Hawari narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'There is no trifle of harming the neighbor.'"
"21134","536 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah gave birth twenty nights after her husband's death, and the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - commanded her to marry."
"21135","537 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi' narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - similar."
"21136","538 - Isma'il ibn Qirat narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Yusuf ibn al-Safar narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: I heard the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: 'There is no harm in the skin of carrion when it is tanned.'"
"21137","539 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Uqbah narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that a woman was given a sheep by a man which had been given in charity to her, so the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - commanded her to accept it."
"21138","Abdullah ibn Abi Labid from Abu Salamah from Umm Salamah. 540 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Abdullah ibn Abi Labid, who said: I heard Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - came to me one day and prayed two rak'ahs after Asr, though I had never seen him pray them, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, what are these two rak'ahs? He said: 'A delegation of Banu Tamim came, and I used to pray two rak'ahs after Zuhr but had not prayed them, so these are they.'"
"21139","Anbasah ibn Ammar al-Madani from Abu Salamah from Umm Salamah - may Allah be pleased with her. 541 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us, my father narrated to us, (Ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Duhaym narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Anbasah ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - bathed, he and a woman of his wives, from a single vessel."
"21140","Khalid ibn Iyas from Abu Salamah from Umm Salamah. 542 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Tha'labah narrated to us, Abu Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Khalid ibn Iyas narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - liked to travel on Thursday."
"21141","543 - Allan ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Iyas, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - liked to travel on Thursday."
"21142","Abu Salih al-Samman from Abu Salamah from Umm Salamah. 544 - Ali ibn Ishaq al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zunbur narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'When one of you sees in his dream what he dislikes, let him spit to his left three times and seek refuge from what he saw.'"
"21143","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah. 545 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Tawbah al-Anbari, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - never fasted a complete month except Sha'ban, which he would join to Ramadan."
"21144","Abd Rabbih from Abu Salamah from Umm Salamah. 546 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd Rabbih, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: Subay'ah gave birth after her husband's death, and two men proposed to her, and they said: She has not become lawful. She mentioned that to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'You have become lawful, so marry whomever you wish.'"
"21145","547 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim narrated to us, from Malik, (Ha). And Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Abd Rabbih ibn Sa'id, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah gave birth half a month after her husband's death, and two men proposed to her, one young and the other old; she inclined to the young one, and the old one said: She has not become lawful, while her family was absent, hoping that when her family came they would prefer him for her. So she came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and he said: 'You have become lawful, so marry whomever you wish.'"
"21146","al-Hatibi from Abu Salamah from Umm Salamah. 548 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Hatibi narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - used to bathe with one of his wives from a single vessel."
"21147","Sa'id al-Maqburi from Abu Salamah from Umm Salamah. 549 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Malik, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Umm Salamah informed him that Subay'ah gave birth half a month after her husband's death."
"21148","Awn ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah from Abu Salamah from Umm Salamah. 550 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah and Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Khayyat narrated to us, both said: Hammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Anbasah narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: 'There is no servant afflicted with an affliction who says: To Allah we belong and to Him we return, O Allah, with You I seek the reward of my affliction, so reward me in it with better than it, except that Allah rewards him in his affliction and grants him better than it afterward.'"
"21149","al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Umm Salamah. 551 - Abu Yahya Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - used to kiss her while fasting."
"21150","552 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Abbadi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dawud al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: 'If among the first things my Lord forbade me and entrusted to me after worship of idols and drinking wine was quarreling with men.'"
"21151","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah from Abu Salamah from Umm Salamah. 553 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: A woman entered upon the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - while he was in the house of Umm Salamah, and said: O Messenger of Allah, what of a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees? Umm Salamah said: Fie upon you, you have disgraced women. She said: Allah is not shy of the truth. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Whoever of you sees that, let her bathe.'"
"21152","554 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah mentions men in everything and does not mention us. So Allah revealed: {Indeed, the Muslim men and Muslim women, the believing men and believing women} the verse to its end."
"21153","555 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (Ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Umm Salamah, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - in a quilt, and I felt what women feel of menstruation. He said: 'That is what has been decreed upon the daughters of Adam.' So I slipped away, set my affair right, then returned. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Come, enter with me into the quilt.' She said: So I entered with him."
"21154","556 - Abbad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Hakim narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah, who said: The husband of Subay'ah bint al-Harith died, and she gave birth days after his death, and the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - commanded her to marry."
"21155","557 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Junadah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Whoever has a sacrifice he intends to slaughter, when the crescent of Dhu al-Hijjah appears, let him not touch anything of his hair nor of his nails until he slaughters.'"
"21156","al-Wazi' ibn Nafi' from Abu Salamah from Umm Salamah. 558 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Jarjarai narrated to us, Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, from al-Wazi', from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: A slave girl of Hassan ibn Thabit entered upon us on the day of Fitr with her hair spread, with a tambourine, singing, and Umm Salamah rebuked her, so the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Leave her, O Umm Salamah, for every people has a festival, and this is our festival day.'"
"21157","Salim Abu al-Nadr from Abu Salamah from Umm Salamah. 559 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and said: I suffer istihadah. He said: 'That is not menstruation; it is only a vein. The woman should sit out the days of her periods, then bathe, then wrap herself with a cloth and pray.'"
"21158","Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Abu Salamah from Umm Salamah. 560 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Bundar narrated to us, (Ha). And Muhammad ibn Salih al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, both said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'Expel the Jews from the Arabian Peninsula.'"
"21159","561 - And with his chain, from her, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - counseled at his death, saying: 'Allah, Allah regarding the Copts of Egypt, for you will prevail over them, and they will be for you a support and helpers in the path of Allah.'"
"21160","Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Umm Salamah. 562 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, (Ha). And Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, both said: Malik narrated to us, from Amr ibn Muslim al-Junda'i, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: 'When the ten enter, whoever intends to sacrifice should not take anything from his hair nor from his nails.'"
"21161","563 - Yahya ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abu Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Amr ibn Muslim al-Junda'i, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - similar."
"21162","564 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Amr ibn Hakam narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Malik, from Amr ibn Muslim, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - similar."
"21163","565 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - similar."
"21164","566 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Abu al-Malih al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Bayan, from Ali ibn Nufayl, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Mahdi was mentioned before the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and he said: 'From the children of Fatimah - may Allah be pleased with her.'"
"21165","Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from Umm Salamah. 567 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from A'ishah and Umm Salamah, who both said: Safiyyah bint Huyayy menstruated before the departure, and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - came to her while she was weeping and said: 'Will she detain us? Had you performed the circumambulation on the Day of Sacrifice?' She said: Yes. He said: 'Then depart.'"
"21166","568 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Urwah, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - came to us while so-and-so was complaining, and said: 'What is this?' We said: We suspect the evil eye for him. He said: 'Will you not seek ruqyah for him from the evil eye?'"
"21167","569 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi' al-Tahhan al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, who said: Makhramah ibn Bukayr informed me, from his father, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, who said: Umm Salamah said: I mentioned the False Messiah one night and sleep did not come to me; in the morning I went to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and informed him, and he said: 'Do not do so, for if he emerges while I am among you, Allah will suffice you through me; and if he emerges after I die, the righteous will suffice you.' Then he stood and mentioned the Dajjal, saying: 'There is no prophet except that he warned his ummah of him, and I warn you of him: he is one-eyed, and Allah is not one-eyed. Lo, the False Messiah is as if his eye were a protruding grape.'"
"21168","570 - Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ali ibn Harb al-Mawsili narrated to us, Harun ibn Imran narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, who said: Umm Salamah narrated to me, who said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - sent me ahead among the weak of his family whom he sent ahead on the night of Muzdalifah. She said: So I threw the pebble at night, then went to Makkah, prayed Fajr there, then returned to Mina."
"21169","571 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Qabisah al-Fazari narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Umm Salamah, that she said to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -: I have not performed the farewell circumambulation. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to her: 'When the people pray Fajr, perform tawaf on your camel from behind the rows, then leave.'"
"21170","Sulayman ibn Yasar from Umm Salamah. 572 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that Abu Hurayrah, Ibn Abbas, and Abu Salamah gathered and discussed the woman who gives birth after her husband's death. Ibn Abbas said: The later of the two terms; Abu Salamah said: When she gives birth, she becomes lawful. Abu Hurayrah said: I am with my nephew's son. So they sent Kurayb to Umm Salamah, and she mentioned the hadith of Subay'ah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - commanded her to marry."
"21171","573 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Malik, from Yahya ibn Said, from Sulayman ibn Yasar: that Ibn Abbas and Abu Salama sent Kurayb, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, to Umm Salama, and then he mentioned something similar."
"21172","574 - Ali narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, (Ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, both saying: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Kurayb, from Umm Salama; and from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Kurayb, from Umm Salama, she said: Subayah bint al-Harith gave birth a few days after the death of her husband, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her to marry."
"21173","575 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mualla ibn Rashid narrated to us, Wahb narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Umm Salama: that Fatimah suffered prolonged non-menstrual bleeding and would wash from a large vessel, then come out with intense yellowness and murkiness, so Umm Salama sought a verdict for her from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: She should wait out the days of her menstruation and abandon prayer in them, and wash in other than that, and pray. Ayyub said: So I said to Sulayman ibn Yasar: May her husband approach her? He said: We only say what we heard."
"21174","576 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abadah ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abu Maryam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, something similar."
"21175","577 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Nafi, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Umm Salama: that Fatimah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I see blood. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her to wash and to perform ablution for every prayer."
"21176","578 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Umm Salama, she said: A woman asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I suffer prolonged bleeding and do not become pure; shall I abandon prayer? He said: No, but leave aside the number of days and nights in which you used to menstruate, then wash, pad yourself with a cloth, and pray."
"21177","579 - Al-Husayn narrated to us, Uthman narrated to us, Abdah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Umm Salama: that she mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the trailing hems of women, and he said: Let them lower a span. She said: Then they would be exposed. He said: Then a cubit, and they must not add beyond it."
"21178","580 - Al-Husayn ibn Mansur al-Rummani narrated to us, al-Muafa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, (Ha). And Sulayman ibn al-Muafa narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Hakim ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, he said: I heard Umm Salama say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: After me there will be a swallowing of the earth in the east, and a swallowing in the west, and a swallowing in the Arabian Peninsula. She said: O Messenger of Allah, will the earth swallow while the righteous are among them? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: When filth becomes predominant among its people."
"21179","581 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: I heard Sulayman ibn Yasar narrating from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake in a state of major impurity not from a wet dream, then wash and continue his fast."
"21180","582 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Said ibn Hafs al-Najjari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar."
"21181","583 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Umm Salama: that a woman was hemorrhaging blood in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so Umm Salama sought a verdict for her from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Let her consider the number of nights and days she used to menstruate in the month before what afflicted her afflicted her, and let her leave prayer for that amount of the month; when she has passed that, let her wash, then pad herself with a cloth, then pray."
"21182","Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah from Umm Salama. 584 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aishah narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah narrated to us, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never prayed them with me except once: he entered one day after Asr and prayed two rakahs, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this prayer; you never used to pray it - has a prayer been revealed after Asr? He said: No, but they are two rakahs I used to pray after Zuhr, and I was distracted from them, so I made them up."
"21183","Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham from Umm Salama. 585 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Habib ibn Abi Thabit informed me: that Abd al-Majid ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Amr and al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed him that they heard Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman reporting that Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him: that when she arrived in Medina, she told them she was the daughter of Umayyah ibn al-Mughirah, but they disbelieved her, saying: How lying are strangers! Until some people set out for Hajj, and they said: Will you write to your family? So she wrote with them, and they returned to Medina affirming her truth, and she rose further in honor with them. She said: When I gave birth to Zaynab, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and proposed to me, so I said: One like me is not married; I am not fertile, I am jealous and have dependents. He said: I am older than you; as for jealousy, Allah will remove it, and as for dependents, they are upon Allah and His Messenger. So he married her. He would come to her saying: Where is Zunab? Until Ammar ibn Yasir came one day and snatched her away, saying: She is keeping the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) away - and she was nursing her. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: Where is Zunab? Qaribah bint Umayyah - who happened to be with her - said: Ammar ibn Yasir took her. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am coming to you tonight. She said: So I got up, laid out my leather mats, took out grains of barley that were in a jar, and brought out fat and prepared porridge for him. She said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spent the night, then in the morning he said when morning came: You have honor with your family; if you wish I will stay seven with you, and if I give seven I will give seven to my wives."
"21184","586 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salama: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he married her, said: If I stay seven with you I will stay seven with my wives."
"21185","587 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham narrated to me, from Umm Salama: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her when he came in to her: You and your family have honor with me; if I stay seven with you I will stay seven with my wives."
"21186","588 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Abd Rabbihi ibn Said, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah and Umm Salama, they both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake junub without a wet dream, then fast."
"21187","589 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Abd Rabbihi ibn Said, from Aishah and Umm Salama, they both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake junub from intercourse without a wet dream, then fast."
"21188","590 - Abd al-Malik ibn Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Jubayr, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Umm Salama: that Zaynab bint the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted protection to Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lowest of the Muslims grants protection on behalf of the Muslims."
"21189","591 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed with Umm Salama three days when he consummated marriage with her, then said: You are not insignificant to your family; if I give you seven I will give seven to my wives."
"21190","592 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Umm Salama: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he married Umm Salama, stayed with her three days, and said: You are not insignificant to your family; if you wish I will give seven for you, and if I give seven for you I will give seven to my wives."
"21191","593 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Shihab informed me, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Umm Salama and Aishah: that dawn would overtake the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was junub from his wives and had not washed, and he would fast."
"21192","594 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah and Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar."
"21193","595 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Burd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, with a similar chain."
"21194","596 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake junub from women without a dream, then remain fasting."
"21195","597 - Al-Husayn narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, Mindal narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, with his chain, the same."
"21196","598 - And al-Husayn ibn Yaqub narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Burd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, with his chain, something similar."
"21197","599 - Muhammad ibn Nuh al-Askari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr ibn Hazm, from his father, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar."
"21198","600 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Musab ibn Thabit narrated to us, from his uncle Amir, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Umm Salama: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed Asr, would leave and pray two rakahs in his house."
"21199","Ubayd ibn Umayr al-Laythi from Umm Salama. 601 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (Ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani and Uthman narrated to us, they said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from his father, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, he said: Umm Salama said: When Abu Salamah died in Medina, I said: You died a stranger in a strange land; I shall weep for you with a weeping that will be talked about. She said: As I was thus, a woman came to me to join me in wailing from al-Said, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met her and said: Do you want to bring Satan into a house Allah has removed him from twice? She said: So I abandoned it and did not weep for him."
"21200","Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah from Umm Salama. 602 - Ibn al-Sumayda narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Kab narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I forbade you from visiting graves, so visit them, for in them there is a lesson for you."
"21201","603 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ubayd al-Qasim ibn Sallam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pause distinctly in his recitation: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate; All praise belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds; the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate; Master of the Day of Judgment."
"21202","604 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (Ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, both saying: Ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was quicker in hastening Zuhr than you, and you delay Asr more than he did."
"21203","Tawus from Umm Salama. 605 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Amr ibn Hisham al-Harrani narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr al-Basri, from Tawus, from Umm Salama: that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, such-and-such good deeds are written for him."
"21204","Mujahid from Umm Salama. 606 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, (Ha). And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, both saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Umm Salama, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my uncle Hisham ibn al-Mughirah used to feed food, uphold kinship, and do this and that; had he met you he would have become Muslim. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He gave for this world alone and its mention, and he never once said: Forgive me on the Day of Recompense."
"21205","607 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar."
"21206","608 - Abu Yahya al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: We would be with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we were in ihram, and a rider would pass by us, so one of us would let down her garment over her face from above her head - and perhaps she said: from above the khimar."
"21207","609 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: Umm Salama said: O Messenger of Allah, we are not given inheritance, nor do we fight so that we are martyred. So Allah revealed: And do not wish for what Allah has favored some of you with over others, to the end of the verse. Then there was revealed: I do not waste the deed of any doer among you, male or female."
"21208","Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Umm Salama. 610 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (Ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, both saying: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Layth, from Ata, from Umm Salama: that she wore a necklace containing small hairs of gold, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw it and disliked it, and turned away from her. So she removed it, and he said: What will secure you from being adorned on the Day of Resurrection in its place with hairs of fire?"
"21209","611 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ali ibn Hamzah al-Ataki narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abdullah al-Razi narrated to us, from Nafi ibn Mihran, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever prays four rakahs before Asr, Allah forbids his body to the Fire. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have seen you pray them and leave them. He said: I am not like any of them."
"21210","612 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Abu Ghassan narrated to us, Jafar al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata, from Umm Salama: that Fatimah came with food of hers to her father while he was on his sleeping mat, so he said: Go and call my two sons and the son of your uncle. She said: So he covered them - or she said: So I turned the cloak over them - then said: O Allah, these are my household and my close kin, so remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly. Umm Salama said: And am I with them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: You are the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and toward - or: upon - good."
"21211","613 - Al-Mamari narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Muhajir, from Thabit ibn Ajlan, from Ata, from Umm Salama: that she used to wear anklets of gold, so she asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Is it treasure? He said: When you pay its zakat, it is not treasure."
"21212","Ikrimah from Umm Salama. 614 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan narrated to us, Qays narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Aishah; and from Abd al-Karim, from Ikrimah, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only forbade gold. We said: O Messenger of Allah, the clasp is adorned with gold? He said: No, unless it be with silver, then smear it with saffron."
"21213","615 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Umm Salama, she said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a blanket, and I menstruated, so he said: Go back, tighten your waist-wrapper over you, then return."
"21214","Kurayb from Umm Salama. 616 - Yahya ibn Uthman narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali informed me, from his father, from Kurayb, he said: People sent me to Umm Salama to ask her: Which days did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fast most? She said: Saturday and Sunday, and he would say: They are festival days of the polytheists, and I love to differ from them."
"21215","Miqsam from Umm Salama. 617 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform witr with five or seven, not separating between them with speech nor with salutation."
"21216","Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan from Umm Salama. 618 - Abu al-Jahm Amr ibn Hazim al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Abd al-Khaliq ibn Zayd ibn Waqid narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, from his father, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no one who wears a garment to show off in it, so people look at him, except that Allah does not look at him until he removes it, whenever he removes it."
"21217","619 - Abu al-Jahm Amr ibn Hazim narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Khaliq ibn Zayd narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, from his father, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever learns knowledge to show off to the scholars and to dispute with the foolish is in the Fire."
"21218","Ata ibn Yasar from Umm Salama. 620 - Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Kathir, from Salim Abu Abdullah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Umm Salama: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is tried with judging between the Muslims, let him not judge while angry."
"21219","621 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Umm Salama: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss while fasting."
"21220","622 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abbad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Abdullah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Umm Salama: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is tried with judging between the Muslims, let him be just among them in his glance, his gesture, his seat, and his sitting place."
"21221","623 - And with it he said: Whoever is tried with judging between the Muslims, let him not raise his voice against one of the two disputants any more than he raises it against the other."
"21222","624 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abbad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Abdullah, from Ataullah ibn Yasar, from Umm Salama: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not cut bread with the knife as the non-Arabs cut it; and when one of you wants to eat meat, let him not cut it with the knife, but let him take it with his hand and bite it with his mouth, for it is more wholesome and more pleasant."
"21223","625 - Ali narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abbad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Abdullah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Umm Salama: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not sniff food as predatory beasts sniff it."
"21224","626 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf informed me, that Ata ibn Yasar informed him, that Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him: that she served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a roasted side, so he ate from it, then stood for prayer and did not perform ablution."
"21225","627 - Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abi Namir, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Umm Salama, she said: In my house this verse was revealed: Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the house, and to purify you thoroughly. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for Fatimah, Hasan, and Husayn, and said: O Allah, my family. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, am I of the household? He said: If Allah wills."
"21226","Abdullah ibn Shaddad from Umm Salama. 628 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu Awn, he said: I am Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had - he said: Marwan sent me to Umm Salama, so I asked her, and she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me having performed ablution, so I handed him a bone with meat, or a shoulder, and he ate, then stood for prayer and did not perform ablution."
"21227","629 - Al-Husayn ibn Jafar al-Qattat narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Misar, from Abu Awn, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"21228","630 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, (Ha). And Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qitrani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, (Ha). And Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Awn, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Umm Salama: she was asked about what fire has altered, and she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a shoulder, then prayed and did not perform ablution."
"21229","631 - Al-Husayn ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Umm Salama: that Asma wept over Jafar, or Hamzah, three days, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her to stop weeping and to apply kohl."
"21230","Ali ibn Husayn from Umm Salama. 632 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from al-Qasim ibn Awf, from Ali ibn Husayn, he said: Umm Salama narrated to us: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while one day resting at midday in her house with a man of his companions conversing, a man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, how much is the sadaqah of such-and-such dates? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Such-and-such. The man said: So-and-so transgressed against me and took from me such-and-such dates, and added a sa. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: How will it be when there strives against you one who transgresses against you more severely than this transgression? The people plunged into talk and the discourse astonished them, until a man among them said: How, O Messenger of Allah, if a man absent from you with his camels, cattle, and crops pays the zakat of his wealth, then the right is exceeded against him - how should he act while absent from you? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever pays the zakat of his wealth with a content soul, seeking thereby the Face of Allah and the Hereafter, not concealing anything of his wealth, and establishes prayer, then pays zakat, then he is wronged regarding the right, so he takes up arms and fights and is killed - he is a martyr."
"21231","Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr from Umm Salama. 633 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub and Abd al-Rahman al-Siraj, from Nafi, from Zayd ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who drinks in a silver vessel only gurgles the fire of Hell in his belly."
"21232","634 - Ali narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Zayd ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar."
"21233","635 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr and Abdah narrated to us, both saying: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Zayd ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar."
"21234","Awf ibn al-Harith ibn al-Tufayl from Umm Salama. 636 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Husayn, from Awf ibn al-Harith ibn al-Tufayl, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, meaning to his wives: The one who is tender to you after me is the truthful, dutiful one. O Allah, give Ibn Awf to drink from al-Salsabil."
"21235","Al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab from Umm Salama, may Allah be pleased with her. 637 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting one day in my house and said: Let no one enter upon me. So I waited, then al-Husayn entered, and I heard the sobbing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) weeping. So I looked, and Husayn was in his lap, or at his side, wiping his head while he wept. So I said: By Allah, I did not know when he entered. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril was in the house and said: Do you love him? I said: As for in this world, yes. He said: Your ummah will kill him in a land called Karbala. So Jibril took some of its soil and showed it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When Husayn was surrounded at his killing, he said: What is the name of this land? They said: Karbala. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke the truth: a land of distress and tribulation."
"21236","Sulayman, freedman of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama. 638 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to me, Said ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Hakam al-Bunani, he said: Sulayman, freedman of Umm Salama, narrated to me, from Umm Salama, she said: A single vessel about half a faraq would be placed for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would begin in it, then I and he would wash together."
"21237","Thabit, freedman of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama. 639 - Ahmad ibn Ma Bahram al-Idhaji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Buhlul ibn Muwarraq narrated to us, Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, Thabit, freedman of Umm Salama, narrated to me, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to me after Asr and prayed two rakahs, so I said: What are these two rakahs, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I used to pray them before Asr, then some people came to me and distracted me, so I prayed them now."
"21238","Nafi, freedman of Ibn Umar, from Umm Salama. 640 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ziyad ibn Saman wrote to me, that Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari informed him, from Nafi, from Umm Salama: that a slave boy of hers divorced a free wife of his with two divorces, so Umm Salama sought a verdict from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: She is forbidden to him until she marries a husband other than him."
"21239","641 - Abd al-Razzaq said: And I heard Abdullah ibn Ziyad narrating that Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed him, from Nafi, from Umm Salama, then he mentioned the same."
"21240","642 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman narrated to us, Abdah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake junub from intercourse, not from a wet dream, then complete his fast."
"21241","643 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yala narrated to us, Anbasah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Nafi, from his father, from Umm Salama: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade qunut in the Fajr prayer."
"21242","644 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, Musa ibn Asim narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Nafi, he said: I heard Umm Salama say: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a blanket, then I slipped out of his blanket, so he said: What is wrong with you? Have you menstruated? I said: Yes. He said: Tighten your waist-wrapper over you and return to where you were."
"21243","Yala ibn Mamlak from Umm Salama. 645 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Yala ibn Mamlak: that he asked Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), about the prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she said: He would pray the last Isha, then glorify Allah, then pray after it whatever Allah willed of the night, then leave and sleep as much as he had prayed, then wake from that sleep of his and pray as much as he had slept; and that last prayer of his would extend until dawn."
"21244","646 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abu Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Ibn Lahiah, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Yala ibn Mamlak, from Umm Salama: that she described the recitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she described a distinct recitation, letter by letter."
"21245","Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ali from Umm Salama. 647 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hajj is the jihad of every weak one."
"21246","648 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ismail ibn Zurarah narrated to us, Ismat ibn Abdullah al-Asadi narrated to us, Abu Maryam narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abu Jafar, from Umm Salama, she said: I had a gazelle of gold, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to give it in charity, so I did."
"21247","Said ibn Marjanah from Umm Salama. 649 - Said ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Tahir ibn Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Sulayman ibn Yasar: that Ibn Marjanah narrated to him, from Umm Salama, that she said: A woman was hemorrhaging blood in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Umm Salama asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about her affair, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let her consider the number of days and nights she used to menstruate before this blood that has come, and their measure in the month, and let her leave prayer for that amount; when she passes that, let her wash, then pad herself with her garment, and pray."
"21248","Abd al-Rahman ibn Shaybah from Umm Salama. 650 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Shaybah narrated to us, he said: I heard Umm Salama say: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Why are we not mentioned in the Quran as men are mentioned? Nothing startled me one day except a recitation upon the pulpit, while I was combing my hair; so I gathered my hair, then went out to my chamber and put my ear at the palm-leaf screen, and he was saying upon the pulpit: O you who believe, Allah says in His Book: The Muslim men and Muslim women, and the believing men and believing women, to the end of the verse."
"21249","Salamah of the children of Umm Salama from Umm Salama. 651 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Salamah, of the children of Umm Salama: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have not heard Allah mention women regarding emigration, so Allah revealed: Indeed Allah does not waste; I do not waste the deed of any doer among you, male or female."
"21250","652 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Salamah, a man of the children of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, she said: Al-Zubayr disputed with a man before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he judged for al-Zubayr. The man said: He only judged for him because he is the son of his aunt. So there was revealed: But no, by your Lord, they will not believe until they make you judge, the verse."
"21251","Abdullah ibn Farrukh from Umm Salama. 653 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Yahya, from Abdullah ibn Farrukh, from Umm Salama: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss while fasting."
"21252","654 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Yahya, from Abdullah ibn Farrukh, from Umm Salama, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss me while I was fasting and he was fasting."
"21253","Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal from Umm Salama. 655 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Umm Salama: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in her house two rakahs after Asr which he had never prayed before nor after."
"21254","656 - Ahmad ibn Musa al-Shami al-Basri narrated to us, Sahl ibn Tammam ibn Bazigh narrated to us, Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allegiance will be given to a man between the Corner and the Maqam, equal to the people of Badr; then the bands of the people of Iraq and the substitutes of the people of Sham will come to him; then an army from the people of Sham will raid them until, when they are at al-Bayda, they are swallowed; a man of Quraysh whose maternal uncles are Kalb will raid them, and they will meet and defeat them. It used to be said: Deprived is he who is deprived of the spoils of Kalb."
"21255","Abdullah ibn Rafi, freedman of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama. 657 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abdullah ibn Rafi, from Umm Salama, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman who braids her hair tightly; shall I undo it for janabah? He said: No; it suffices you to take with your two hands handfuls, then pour water over your skin, and you become pure."
"21256","658 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, (Ha). And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, both saying: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Said ibn Abi Said, from Abdullah ibn Rafi, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"21257","659 - Al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Mujawwiz al-Basri narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Maqburi, from Abdullah ibn Rafi, from Umm Salama, she said: Umm Sulaym said: O Messenger of Allah, does a woman have a wet dream? He said: When yellow water comes down, let her wash."
"21258","660 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, (Ha). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Raqashi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Rafi narrated to me, he said: I heard Umm Salama say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When dinner is present and prayer is present, begin with dinner."
"21259","661 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me, that Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj narrated to him, from al-Qasim ibn Abbas al-Hashimi, from Abdullah ibn Rafi, from Umm Salama, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I am your forerunner at the Hawd; beware that none of you comes and is driven away as a stray camel is driven away, so I say: What is this? And it is said: You do not know what they innovated after you. So I say: Away."
"21260","662 - Al-Sarraj, he is al-Hasan ibn Ali, narrated to us, he said: Al-Fadl ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Rafi, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"21261","663 - Abu Yahya al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Abdullah ibn Rafi, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You dispute before me, and I am only a human; I judge between you only according to what I hear from you. So whomever I judge for him anything of his brothers right, I am only cutting for him a piece of the Fire."
"21262","664 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Ilyas, from Abdullah ibn Rafi, from Umm Salama: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he performed ablution, would run his fingers through his beard."
"21263","665 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Hakim, from Abdullah ibn Rafi, from Umm Salama, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, why are we not mentioned in the Quran as men are mentioned? Nothing startled me except a call upon the pulpit, while I was combing my hair; so I gathered my hair, then put my ear at the palm-leaf screen, and heard him saying: The Muslim men and Muslim women, the verse."
"21264","666 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Musa ibn Jubayr, from Abdullah ibn Rafi, freedman of Umm Salama: that Umm Salama said: The most I knew of wealth brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a leather bag containing eight hundred dirhams."
"21265","667 - Abdan narrated to us, Said ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn Habib, from a freedman of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cupping in the head is a remedy for madness, leprosy, night-blindness, vitiligo, and headache."
"21266","What Amir ibn Abi Umayyah, brother of Umm Salama, narrated from Umm Salama. 668 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Amir, brother of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake junub, then fast that day."
"21267","669 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Amir, brother of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake junub, then wash and fast."
"21268","670 - Abu Harun al-Shirini narrated to us, Abd al-Malik al-Juddi narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah and Amr ibn Murrah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Amir, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar."
"21269","671 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Abu Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Amir, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar."
"21270","672 - Abu Yahya al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Amir, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar."
"21271","Abdullah ibn Abi Umayyah, brother of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama. 673 - Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbadah narrated to us, Yaqub al-Zuhri narrated to us, al-Muttalib ibn Kathir narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn Musa narrated to us, from Musab ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Umayyah, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw freedmen of Abu Jahl in Paradise. Then when Ikrimah became Muslim, he said: He is this one."
"21272","674 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu al-Muafa al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah, brother of Umm Salama, he said: I heard Umm Salama say: Abu Bakr set out in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) trading to Busra; Abu Bakr's attachment to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not prevent him, out of his eagerness for his share of traveling for trade - and that was because of their admiration for the earning of trade and their love of trade; nor did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prevent Abu Bakr from traveling in his trade out of his love for his companionship and his fondness for Abu Bakr, for he admired his companionship, due to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) approving trade and admiring it."
"21273","Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Umayyah from Umm Salama. 675 - Al-Mamari narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, my father narrated to us, (Ha). And Abu al-Zinba narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, both saying: Abdullah ibn Abi al-Samh narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Umayyah, from Umm Salama: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from what fire has touched."
"21274","Nabhan, freedman of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama. 676 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: Nabhan, mukatab of Umm Salama, narrated to us, from Umm Salama, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the mukatab has what he can pay, veil yourself from him."
"21275","677 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Qabisah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from a mukatab of Umm Salama called Nabhan, from Umm Salama, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the mukatab finds what he can pay, veil yourself from him."
"21276","678 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, (Ha). And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, both saying: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from Nabhan, from Umm Salama, she said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Maymunah was with him, when Ibn Umm Maktum approached. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Veil yourselves from him. So we said: O Messenger of Allah, is he not blind, neither seeing us nor recognizing us? He said: Even so, do you two not see him?"
"21277","679 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam al-Ijli narrated to us, Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Nabhan, from Umm Salama: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would touch her intimately while she was menstruating with a waist-wrapper over her."
"21278","Abu Kathir, freedman of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama. 680 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (Ha). And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, both saying: Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, Huraym ibn Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Abu Kathir, freedman of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Say at the Maghrib adhan: O Allah, with the coming of Your night, the departure of Your day, the voices of Your callers, and the presence of Your prayers, forgive me. And when she woke in the night restless, she would say: My Lord, forgive, have mercy, and guide to the straightest path."
"21279","681 - Al-Husayn narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Humaydah bint Abi Kathir, from her father Abu Kathir, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar."
"21280","Ikrimah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith from Umm Salama. 682 - Hajjaj ibn Imran narrated to us, Yahya ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sayfi, from Ikrimah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like the hadith that follows it."
"21281","683 - Al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad ibn Qumayr narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn Sayfi informed me, that Ikrimah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith informed him, from Umm Salama: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) swore not to enter upon some of his wives for a month; when twenty-nine days passed he came to them in the morning - or in the evening - and it was said: O Messenger of Allah, you swore not to enter upon them for a month. He said: A month may be twenty-nine days."
"21282","684 - Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Sarraj narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Mukram narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sayfi informed me, from Ikrimah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, he informed him, that Umm Salama informed him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) swore not to enter upon some of his wives for a month; when twenty-nine days passed he came to them in the morning - or in the evening - and it was said to him: O Prophet of Allah, you swore not to enter for a month. He said: A month is twenty-nine days."
"21283","Safinah, freedman of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama. 685 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, from a freedman of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say at the end of prayer: O Allah, I ask You for wholesome provision, accepted deed, and beneficial knowledge."
"21284","686 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, from a freedman of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, she said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose in the morning and prayed the Fajr prayer, he mentioned something similar."
"21285","687 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, something similar."
"21286","688 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Mamar narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, from a freedman of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar."
"21287","689 - Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, from Safinah, freedman of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar."
"21288","690 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Safinah, freedman of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, she said: The general bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at his death was: Prayer, and what your right hands possess."
"21289","691 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Khalil, from Safinah, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar."
"21290","692 - Al-Husayn narrated to us, Uthman narrated to us, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Sad ibn Said narrated to us, Umar ibn Kathir narrated to me, from Safinah, freedman of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no servant afflicted with a calamity who says: To Allah we belong and to Him we return; O Allah, reward me in my calamity and replace for me better than it, except that Allah rewards him in his calamity and replaces for him better than it. When Abu Salamah died, I said: Who is better than Abu Salamah, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Then it was resolved for me, so I said it, and I married the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"21291","693 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Ibn Abdullah, he said: Safinah, freedman of Umm Salama, narrated to me, from Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels do not accompany a caravan in which there is a bell."
"21292","Abdullah ibn al-Hasan from Umm Salama. 694 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawal narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Hasan, from Umm Salama: that she swore regarding a slave boy of hers who had sought her manumission, saying: May Allah not free her from the Fire if she ever frees him. Then she remained what Allah willed, then said: Glory be to Allah, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever swears an oath then sees better than it, let him expiate for his oath, then do that which is better. So she freed the slave, then expiated for her oath."
"21293","695 - Al-Buhturi ibn Muhammad al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Hasan, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lacks one of three has nothing to count upon: piety restraining him from prohibitions, or forbearance with which he holds back from the fool, or character with which he lives among people."
"21294","Abu Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Zamah from Umm Salama. 696 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Shaybani narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Athmah narrated to us, Musa ibn Yaqub al-Zamai narrated to us, from Hashim ibn Hashim ibn Utbah, from Abdullah ibn Wahb ibn Zamah, he said: Umm Salama informed me: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered Fatimah, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn, then brought them under his garment, then said: O Allah, these are my family. Umm Salama said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, admit me with them. He said: You are of my family."
"21295","697 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us, Musa ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Hashim ibn Hashim narrated to me, from Wahb ibn Abdullah ibn Zamah, he said: Umm Salama informed me: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lay down one day for sleep, then woke heavy in spirit, then lay down and slept, then woke with red soil in his hand turning it over. So I said: What is this soil, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Jibril informed me that this one - Husayn - will be killed in the land of Iraq. So I said to Jibril: Show me the soil of the land in which he will be killed; so this is its soil."
"21296","698 - Abdullah ibn al-Jarud al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Ishaq, from Hashim ibn Hashim, from Abdullah ibn Wahb ibn Zamah, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"21297","699 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (Ha). And Abu Yahya al-Dari narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, both saying: Waki narrated to us, from Zamah ibn Salih, from al-Zuhri, from Wahb ibn Abdullah ibn Zamah, from Umm Salama, she said: Abu Bakr set out trading to Busra a year before the death of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with Numayman and Suwaybit ibn Harmalah; both had witnessed Badr. Numayman was in charge of provisions, so Suwaybit - a jesting man - said to him: Feed me. He said: Until your companion comes. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"21298","700 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abdullah ibn Zamah, from Umm Salama, she said: My menstruation came upon me while I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I slipped away. He said to me: O Umm Salama, perhaps you have menstruated. I said: Yes. He said: Return and lie down. She said: So I returned and lay down, with nothing between me and him of the waist-wrapper beyond the knees."
"21299","701 - Ismail ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Musa ibn Yaqub, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Wahb ibn Zamah: that his father informed him, that Umm Salama informed him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would enter upon his wives in the morning and greet them; and there was a woman among them who had honey, and whenever he entered upon her she would present some of it to him, so he stayed with her accordingly; and Aishah and Hafsah were affected by that, so when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon them they said: We smell from you the odor of maghafir. So he abandoned that honey."
"21300","Wahb ibn Abdullah ibn Zamah ibn al-Aswad from Umm Salama. 702 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Musa ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Ibn Abi Ubaydah ibn Abdullah ibn Zamah informed me, from his father, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you drink milk, rinse from it, for it has richness."
"21301","703 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Musa ibn Yaqub, he said: Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah ibn Zamah informed me, from his father, from Umm Salama, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you drink milk, rinse from it, for it has richness."
"21302","704 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Khalil ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah ibn Zamah, from his father, from Umm Salama, she said: When it was the evening of the Day of Sacrifice, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw Wahb ibn Zamah and a man from the family of Abu Umayyah wearing shirts, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Wahb: Have you performed ifadah, O Abu Abdullah? He said: No. He said: Remove your shirt. Wahb said: Why, O Messenger of Allah? He said: This is a day in which I permit you, when you have stoned the Jamrat al-Aqabah, to exit from everything forbidden to you of the rites of Hajj except women; but if evening comes upon one of you and he has not performed ifadah, he remains in his state as muhrim until he performs ifadah."
"21303","Wahb, freedman of Abu Ahmad, from Umm Salama. 705 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, (Ha). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Wahb, freedman of Abu Ahmad, from Umm Salama: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to her while she was veiling herself, and said: One wrap, not two wraps."
"21304","Abd al-Rahman ibn Said ibn Yarbu from Umm Salama. 706 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar al-Akhnas narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Said ibn Yarbu, from Umm Salama: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his wives in the year of the Farewell Hajj: This is the Hajj, then remaining upon mats."
"21305","Umm Sabit from Umm Salama. 707 - Al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Muawiyah narrated to us, from Sufyan and Shayban, from Jabir, from Ibn Sabit, from Umm Salama, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to eat while junub, he performed his ablution for prayer."
"21306","708 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abu Shaybah narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Umm Salama, she said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Is jihad upon women? He said: Their jihad is here - and he gestured with his hand toward Mecca."
"21307","Al-Saib, freedman of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama. 709 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qitrani narrated to us, Kamil ibn Talhah narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Darraj, from al-Saib, freedman of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best prayer of women is in the innermost of their houses."
"21308","710 - Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith: that Darraj informed him, from al-Saib: that he heard Umm Salama, may Allah be pleased with her, heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any woman who removes her clothes in other than her house, Allah tears His veil from her."
"21309","Al-Sab ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Umayyah from Umm Salama. 711 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Al-Layth narrated to me, Yahya ibn Sulaym ibn Zayd, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to us, from al-Sab ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Umayyah, Umm Salama narrated to me, that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will come upon people a time in which the truthful is disbelieved, the liar is believed, the trustworthy is betrayed, the treacherous is trusted, a man testifies though he is not asked to testify, and swears though he is not asked to swear, and the happiest of people with this world will be Luka ibn Luka, who does not believe in Allah and His Messenger."
"21310","Qabisah ibn Dhuayb from Umm Salama. 712 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan al-Missisi narrated to us, (Ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, al-Musayyib ibn Wadih narrated to us, they said: Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Abu Salamah when his sight had fixed, so he closed it and said: When the soul is taken, the sight follows it. So some of his family cried loudly, and he said: Do not supplicate against yourselves except with good, for the angels say amen to what you say. Then he said: O Allah, forgive Abu Salamah, raise his rank among the guided, replace him in his offspring among those who remain, forgive us and him, O Lord of the worlds; O Allah, expand for him in his grave and light it for him."
"21311","713 - Muhammad ibn Isa al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muthanna ibn Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Khalid al-Khuzai, from Abu Qilabah, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb, from Umm Salama: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) closed the eyes of Abu Salamah."
"21312","714 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim narrated to us, Kathir ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Makhlad ibn Hilal, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to me, from Abu Qilabah, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb, from Umm Salama: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Abu Salamah, and he mentioned something like the hadith of al-Fazari."
"21313","Abu Sufyan from Umm Salama. 715 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Bishr ibn Ubays narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Arabi narrated to me, from Kharijah ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Abi Sufyan, from his father, from Umm Salama: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In heaven there are two angels, one commands sternness and the other commands gentleness, and each is correct: Jibril and Mikail; and two prophets, one commands gentleness and the other commands sternness, and each is correct - and he mentioned Ibrahim and Nuh; and I have two companions, one commands gentleness and the other sternness, and each is correct - and he mentioned Abu Bakr and Umar."
"21314","Muslim ibn Sulaym from Umm Salama. 716 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Ishaq ibn Abi Farwah: that Muslim ibn Sulaym narrated to him, from Umm Salama: that a sheep of theirs died, and they did not reach its slaughter before it died, and that reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: If only you had benefited from its hide."
"21315","Asim ibn Abi Ubayd from Umm Salama. 717 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Musab ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Asim ibn Abi Ubaydah, from Umm Salama, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he used to supplicate with these words: O Allah, You are the First, nothing before You, and You are the Last, nothing after You; I seek refuge in You from every creature whose forelock is in Your Hand, and I seek refuge in You from sin and laziness, and from the punishment of the Fire, and from the punishment of the grave, and from the trial of wealth and the trial of poverty, and I seek refuge in You from sinfulness and debt; O Allah, purify my heart of sins as You purified the white garment of filth; O Allah, distance me from my sins as You distanced between the east and the west; this is what Muhammad asked his Lord; O Allah, I ask You for the best of asking, the best of supplication, the best of success, the best of deeds, the best of reward, the best of life, and the best of death; make me firm, weight my scales, establish my faith, raise my rank, accept my prayer, and forgive my sins; and I ask You for the highest ranks of Paradise, Amen; O Allah, I ask You for the beginnings of good, its endings, its comprehensive forms, its first and its last, its outward and its inward, and the highest ranks of Paradise, Amen; O Allah, save me from the Fire, and the forgiveness of night and day, and the righteous abode of Paradise, Amen; O Allah, I ask You for a safe deliverance from the Fire, and admit me to Paradise secure; O Allah, I ask You to bless me in myself, in my hearing, in my sight, in my spirit, in my character, in my form, in my family, in my life, and in my death; O Allah, accept my good deeds, and I ask You for the highest ranks of Paradise, Amen."
"21316","718 - Al-Husayn ibn Ja'far al-Qattat al-Kufi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Talhi narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, from 'Uthman ibn Talhah, Abu 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Umm Salamah, that she said on the day 'A'ishah died: Today the most beloved person in this world to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has died, then she said: I seek Allah's forgiveness, except her father."
"21317","And those who narrated from Umm Salamah among the people of Kufah. Masruq ibn al-Ajda' from Umm Salamah. 719 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Masruq, from Umm Salamah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Among my Companions are some who will never see me after I die. Then 'Umar came and entered upon her and said: I adjure you by Allah, am I one of them? She said: No, and I will never declare anyone free of blame after you, ever. Then 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, wept."
"21318","720 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ghanm ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Basri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah al-Dashtaki narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Masruq, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"21319","721 - 'Allan ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Dinar narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Shaqiq, from Masruq, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"21320","Abu Wa'il Shaqiq ibn Salamah from Umm Salamah. 722 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you attend the dying person, speak good, for the angels say Amen to what you say."
"21321","723 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is afflicted by a calamity, let him say: O Allah, reward me in my calamity and grant me better than it in return. When Abu Salamah died, I said: Who will Allah grant me in return after Abu Salamah? She said: So Allah granted me better than him, Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"21322","724 - Al-Husayn narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us. And al-Husayn narrated to us, 'Uthman narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Umm Salamah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Among my Companions are some who will never see me after I leave them."
"21323","725 - Muhammad ibn Husayn al-Hannat narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Harb al-Mawsili narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Wasil, from Abu Wa'il, he said: Umm Salamah said, when Abu Salamah died, I said: O Messenger of Allah, what should I say? He said: Say: O Allah, forgive him and grant me a beneficial replacement from him. So I said it, and He granted me the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in return."
"21324","'Amir ibn Sharahil al-Sha'bi from Umm Salamah. 726 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Sha'bi, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never left my house in the morning except that he raised his gaze to the sky and said: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from going astray or being led astray, from slipping or being caused to slip, from wronging or being wronged, from being ignorant or being treated with ignorance."
"21325","727 - Ali narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Sha'bi, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to the hadith of Shu'bah."
"21326","728 - Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Idris al-Awdi, from Mansur, from al-Sha'bi, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"21327","729 - Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Jarud narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Hakam ibn Zibyan al-Basri narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Zayd, from al-Sha'bi, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"21328","730 - Khattab ibn Sa'd al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Humayd ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, Mu'ammal narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur and 'Asim, from al-Sha'bi, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"21329","731 - Al-Ma'mari narrated to us, 'Uqbah narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Mansur, from al-Sha'bi, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"21330","732 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Abidah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Sha'bi, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"21331","Kulthum al-Khuza'i from Umm Salamah. 733 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, 'Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Jami' ibn Shaddad, from Kulthum al-Khuza'i, from Umm Salamah, that she used to delouse the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then Zaynab, the wife of Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, came and she began speaking to me and I speaking to her, and I raised my gaze to her, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Attend to your delousing, for you are not speaking to her with your eyes. Zaynab said: So she began complaining of the narrowness of the dwelling, and he said: This is as the wife of 'Uthman ibn Maz'un did; what she settled in did not suffice her until it came down upon her head. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So it is for whoever marks out a plot in Madinah among the emigrant women; hers is her plot, so she inherited her share of the house of Abdullah, and she secured her house in Madinah."
"21332","Al-Muhajir ibn al-Qibtiyyah from Umm Salamah. 734 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from al-Muhajir ibn al-Qibtiyyah, he said: We entered upon Umm Salamah, and she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One seeking refuge will seek refuge at the House, then an army will be sent against him, until when they are at a desert plain of the earth they will be swallowed up. I said: O Prophet of Allah, what of one who was unwilling? He said: He will be swallowed up with them, but he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection according to what was in himself."
"21333","735 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Asad al-'Ammi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, Abu Yunus al-Qushayri narrated to us, from al-Muhajir ibn al-Qibtiyyah, he said: I heard Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"21334","736 - Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Abu Yunus al-Bahili, from al-Muhajir, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"21335","Abu 'Abdullah al-Jadali from Umm Salamah. 737 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Fitr ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu 'Abdullah al-Jadali, he said: Umm Salamah said: O Abu 'Abdullah, is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reviled among you? I said: And who would revile the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: Is not 'Ali reviled, and whoever loves him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to love him?"
"21336","738 - Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Awn ibn Salamah narrated to us. And al-Qattat narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Salih narrated to us, both said: 'Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Abu 'Abdullah al-Jadali, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"21337","739 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Adami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ya'la al-Aslami narrated to us, from Sa'd al-Iskaf, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu 'Abdullah al-Jadali, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I hate the woman who leaves her house trailing her train, complaining of her husband."
"21338","Yahya ibn al-Jazzar from Umm Salamah. 740 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, he said: Some people among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Umm Salamah, and they said: O Mother of the Believers, narrate to us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: His open conduct and his secret were the same. Then she regretted it and said: I have disclosed the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he entered, I informed him, and he said: You did well."
"21339","741 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, both said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray witr with thirteen, then when he grew old and weak he prayed witr with seven."
"21340","Abu Salih, the freedman of Talhah ibn 'Ubaydullah, from Umm Salamah. 742 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, 'Arim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Maymun Abu Hamzah, from Abu Salih, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a boy of hers praying, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Soil your face, O Rabah."
"21341","743 - Ali narrated to us, 'Amr ibn 'Awn narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Abu Salih, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"21342","744 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Qays narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Abu Salih, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"21343","745 - 'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, Abu Hammam narrated to us, from Hudbah ibn al-Minhal, from Maymun, from Abu Salih, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"21344","Al-Ma'rur ibn Suwayd from Umm Salamah. 746 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Layth, from 'Alqamah ibn Marthad, from al-Ma'rur ibn Suwayd, from Umm Salamah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whatever Allah transformed, it had neither offspring nor progeny."
"21345","747 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Mawsili narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us. And Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Layth, from 'Alqamah ibn Marthad, from al-Ma'rur ibn Suwayd, he said: I heard Umm Salamah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When sins appear openly in my ummah, Allah will envelop them with punishment. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will there not be righteous people among the people on that day? He said: Yes. I said: Then what will become of those? He said: What befalls the people will befall them, then they will pass on to forgiveness from Allah and pleasure; the wording is the hadith of Abu al-Rabi'."
"21346","A person from Umm Salamah. 748 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan narrated to us, Kamil Abu al-'Ala' narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from a person, from Umm Salamah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) applied depilatory paste, he would begin with his pubic region, for he is the one who attends to it."
"21347","Hassan ibn al-Mukhariq from Umm Salamah. 749 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, 'Uthman narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Hassan al-Mukhariq, he said: Umm Salamah said: A daughter of mine complained, so I prepared nabidh for her in her jug, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered while it was fermenting, and he said: What is this? I said: My daughter complained, so I prepared this nabidh for her. He said: Allah has not placed your cure in what He has forbidden to you."
"21348","Hakim ibn Sa'd from Umm Salamah. 750 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, 'Uthman narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ja'far ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hakim ibn Sa'd, from Umm Salamah, she said, this verse: Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the House, and to purify you thoroughly, was revealed concerning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and 'Ali, and Fatimah, and al-Hasan, and al-Husayn."
"21349","Rib'i ibn Hirash from Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her. 751 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while his face was gloomy, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, why do I see your face gloomy? He said: The dinars that were brought to us; I forgot them in the fold of my bedding, I was made to forget to distribute them before evening."
"21350","752 - Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya ibn Dawud al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Yazid ibn Mardaniyah narrated to us, Ruqayyah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, from Rib'i, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"21351","Mundhir al-Thawri from Umm Salamah. 753 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-'Assal al-Asbahani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Ja'far al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Jami' ibn Abi Rashid, from Mundhir Abu Ya'la, from Umm Salamah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry, his face would turn red."
"21352","Salih ibn Zayd from Umm Salamah. 754 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, 'Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, both said: Musa al-Juhani narrated to us, from Salih ibn Zayd, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Sit at the door and let no one come in to me. So I stood at the door when al-Husayn came, while he was a young servant boy, and I went to take hold of him but the boy beat me to it and entered upon his grandfather. I said: O Prophet of Allah, may Allah make me your ransom, you commanded me that no one should come in to you, yet your son came and I went to take hold of him but he beat me to it. When that lasted long, I looked in from the door and found you turning something over with your hand while your tears flowed and the child was upon your belly. He said: Yes, Jibril came to me and informed me that my ummah will kill him, and he brought me the soil upon which he will be killed, and it is that which I am turning over with my hand."
"21353","Zirr ibn Hubaysh from Umm Salamah. 755 - Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf narrated to us, Yahya ibn Khidham al-Saqati narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i narrated to us, 'Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us. And Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-'Abbadi narrated to us, they said: al-Hakam ibn Marwan al-Darir narrated to us, Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from 'Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Umm Salamah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Among my Companions are some who will not see me after I die."
"21354","Nufay' ibn al-Harith from Umm Salamah. 756 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yusayr ibn Surayj narrated to us, from Nufay' ibn al-Harith, from Umm Salamah, she said: We never sifted flour for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at all."
"21355","Sa'id ibn Wahb from Umm Salamah. 757 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Wahb, or from his brother, from Umm Salamah, that a sheep of theirs died, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not benefit from its hide?"
"21356","Malik ibn Ja'wanah from Umm Salamah. 758 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Musa ibn Qays narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from 'Iyad ibn 'Iyad, from Malik ibn Ja'wanah, he said: I heard Umm Salamah say: 'Ali was upon the truth; whoever followed him followed the truth, and whoever abandoned him abandoned the truth, a covenant already covenanted before this day of his."
"21357","'Atiyyah Abu al-Mu'addil from his father from Umm Salamah. 759 - Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas narrated to us, Hawdhah narrated to us, both said: 'Awf narrated to us. And al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Abu Zufar Abd al-Salam ibn Mutahhar narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from 'Awf, from 'Atiyyah Abu al-Mu'addil, from his father, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) embraced 'Ali with one hand and Fatimah with one hand, and drew over them a black khamisah that was upon him, and kissed 'Ali and Fatimah, and said: O Allah, to You, not to the Fire, I and my household. Umm Salamah said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, and I? He said: And you."
"21358","And those who narrated from Umm Salamah among the people of Basrah. Dabbah ibn Mihsan al-'Anazi from Umm Salamah. 760 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Abu 'Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, both said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Dabbah ibn Mihsan al-'Anazi, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be rulers, so they will be recognized and denounced; whoever recognizes is absolved, and whoever denounces is safe, but whoever is pleased and follows. They said: Shall we not fight them? He said: No, as long as they pray."
"21359","761 - Abu Yahya al-Razi narrated to us, Zunayj Abu Ghassan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Razi narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from Hisham, from al-Hasan, from Dabbah ibn Mihsan, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"21360","762 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us. And Mu'adh narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, both said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, al-Mu'alla ibn Ziyad and Hisham narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Dabbah ibn Mihsan, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"21361","763 - Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari and al-Husayn ibn Muhhan narrated to us, both said: Zakariya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hibban ibn Aghlab ibn Tamim al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from his father, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, from Dabbah ibn Mihsan, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the desert when a caller called out to him: O Messenger of Allah. So he turned but saw no one, then he turned and there was a tied gazelle. She said: Come near me, O Messenger of Allah. So he drew near to her and said: Your need? She said: I have two fawns in that mountain, so release me until I go and suckle them, then return to you. He said: And will you do so? She said: May Allah punish me with the punishment of the collectors if I do not. So he released her, and she went and suckled her two fawns, then returned, so he tied her up, and the Bedouin awoke and said: Do you have a need, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes, release this one. So he released her, and she went out running, saying: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah."
"21362","'Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab from Umm Salamah. 764 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim and Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated to us, both said: Sallam ibn Abi Muti' narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab narrated to us, he said: We entered upon Umm Salamah, and she brought out for us a bundle containing hair of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dyed with henna, and she said: This is of the hair of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"21363","765 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Dinar, from 'Uthman ibn Abdullah, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"21364","Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah from Umm Salamah. 766 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Mu'alla al-Asadi, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Umm Salamah, she said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was fasting, he would begin with drink, and he would not gulp; he would drink two or three times."
"21365","767 - Abu 'Umar al-Darir narrated to us, Ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Mu'alla al-Maliki, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not gulp in his drink, two or three times."
"21366","Shahr ibn Hawshab from Umm Salamah. Zubayd al-Yami from Shahr ibn Hawshab. 768 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Isra'il narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, that the verse was revealed in her house: Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the House, and to purify you thoroughly, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and 'Ali, and Fatimah, and al-Hasan, and al-Husayn were there. So he took a cloak and covered them with it, then said: O Allah, these are my household, so remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly. I said, while I was at the threshold of the door: O Messenger of Allah, am I with them? He said: You are upon good and toward good."
"21367","769 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hilal ibn Miqlas narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"21368","770 - 'Abdan narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"21369","771 - Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Siraj narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Husayn narrated to us, Ja'far al-Ahmar narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from Zubayd, from Shahr, from Umm Salamah, the same."
"21370","Abu Ka'b, keeper of the palm stalks, from Shahr. 772 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Ka'b narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion."
"21371","773 - Aslam ibn Sahl and 'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both said: al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-A'raj narrated to us, Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Asbat, from al-Suddi, from Bilal ibn Mirdas, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me, then Fatimah brought him a dish of kharirah and placed it before him. He said to me: Call for me your husband and your two sons. So I called them, and they ate with a Khaybari cloak beneath them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered the cloak over them, then said: These are my household and my close kin, so remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly."
"21372","Thabit al-Bunani from Shahr ibn Hawshab. 774 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Musa ibn Khalaf narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite this verse: Indeed it is a deed not righteous."
"21373","775 - Ali narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"21374","776 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Talut ibn 'Abbad narrated to us, Harun ibn Musa narrated to us, from Thabit, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"21375","777 - 'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn 'Ubayd ibn 'Aqil narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Umar al-Bahili narrated to us, 'Abbas ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this word: Indeed it is a deed not righteous."
"21376","778 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this word: Indeed it is a deed not righteous."
"21377","Ali ibn Zayd from Shahr ibn Hawshab. 779 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Fatimah: Bring me your husband and your two sons. So she brought them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast over them a Fadak cloak, then placed his hand upon them and said: O Allah, these are the family of Muhammad, so place Your prayers and Your blessings upon the family of Muhammad, for You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. Umm Salamah said: So I lifted the cloak to enter with them, but he pulled it from my hand and said: You are upon good."
"21378","'Uqbah ibn Abdullah al-Rifa'i from Shahr ibn Hawshab. 780 - Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim al-'Askari narrated to us, Hawtharah ibn Ashras narrated to us, 'Uqbah ibn Abdullah al-Rifa'i narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Fatimah: Bring me your husband and your two sons. So she brought them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast a cloak over them, then said: These are the family of Muhammad, so place Your prayers and Your blessings upon the family of Muhammad, as You placed them upon the family of Ibrahim; You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."
"21379","Al-Hakam ibn 'Utaybah from Shahr ibn Hawshab. 781 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us. And al-Husayn narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani and 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn 'Amr, from al-Hakam, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every intoxicant and enervator."
"21380","Yazid, freedman of al-Sahba', from Shahr. 782 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya and 'Uthman narrated to us, both said: Waki' narrated to us, from Yazid, freedman of al-Sahba', from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), His saying: And they will not disobey you in what is right, he said: Wailing."
"21381","Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Shahr. 783 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur narrated to us, Husayn al-Ashqar narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a garment and covered 'Ali and Fatimah and al-Hasan and al-Husayn with it, then recited this verse: Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the House, and to purify you thoroughly."
"21382","Zayd al-'Ammi from Shahr. 784 - Muhammad ibn Nuh al-'Askari narrated to us, Yahya ibn 'Allan narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abu al-Fadl al-Qaysi, from Zayd al-'Ammi, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he recited: A deed not righteous."
"21383","Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram from Shahr ibn Hawshab. 785 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, he said: I heard Umm Salamah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to often say: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, do hearts indeed turn? He said: Yes, Allah has not created any human of the children of Adam except that his heart is between two fingers of the fingers of Allah; if He wills He keeps it straight, and if He wills He turns it astray. So we ask Allah our Lord not to turn our hearts astray after He has guided us, and we ask Him to grant us mercy from Himself; indeed He is the Bestower. I said: O Messenger of Allah, then teach me a supplication with which I may supplicate for myself. He said: Say: O Allah, forgive my sin, remove the anger of my heart, and shield me from the misguiding trials."
"21384","786 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, he said: I heard Umm Salamah, when the news of the death of al-Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, came, curse the people of Iraq, and say: They killed him, may Allah kill them; they humiliated him and disgraced him, may Allah curse them. For I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, came to him, then he mentioned the hadith."
"21385","787 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, he said: I heard Umm Salamah narrate that Fatimah came complaining of service, and she said: O Messenger of Allah, my hands have become calloused from the millstone, bread at one time and dough at another. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: If Allah grants you anything it will come to you; I shall guide you to something better than that: when you take to your bed, glorify Allah thirty-three times, praise Allah thirty-three times, and magnify Allah thirty-four times, for that is better for you than a servant. And when you pray the dawn prayer, say: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise; He gives life and causes death; in His Hand is good, and He is over all things Powerful, ten times after the dawn prayer and ten times after the sunset prayer. For each one of them ten good deeds are recorded and ten sins are erased, and each one of them is like freeing a slave from the children of Isma'il; no sin written that day can persist but it erases it, except that it be polytheism: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner. And it guards you, between your saying it in the morning until you say it in the evening, from every devil and from every thing."
"21386","Abu 'Uthman from Umm Salamah. 788 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, from his father, from Abu 'Uthman, he said: Umm Salamah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was speaking to a man, and he said: O Umm Salamah, who is this? I said: Dihyah al-Kalbi. And I did not know that he was Jibril until I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrate to his Companions what had passed between them. I said to Abu 'Uthman: Who narrated this to you? He said: Usamah ibn Zayd."
"21387","And those who narrated from Umm Salamah among the people of Egypt. Abu Qays, freedman of 'Amr ibn al-'As, from Umm Salamah. 789 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, Musa ibn 'Ulayy ibn Rabah al-Lakhmi narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Qays, that Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As sent him to Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), to ask her: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting? If she says: No, then say to her: 'A'ishah narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting. Abu Qays said: So I came to her, and she said: Free or slave? I said: Rather a slave. She said: Come near. So I drew near and said: Abdullah ibn 'Amr sent me to you to ask you: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting? She said: No. So I said: 'A'ishah narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting. She said: Perhaps he could not restrain himself for love of her."
"21388","Aslam Abu 'Imran from Umm Salamah. 790 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Haywah ibn Shurayh, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Aslam Abu 'Imran, he said: I performed Hajj and met Umm Salamah, and she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever of you performs Hajj, let him enter ihram for both together, with Hajj and 'Umrah."
"21389","791 - And Harun ibn Mamluk al-Misri narrated to us, al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, the same."
"21390","792 - Al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abu Salih Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Aslam Abu 'Imran, he said: I performed Hajj with my master and entered upon Umm Salamah, and she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Enter ihram, O ummah of Muhammad, with Hajj and 'Umrah."
"21391","Al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah from Umm Salamah. 793 - Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Hammad al-Barbari narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Adam narrated to us, both said: Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, from Muslim al-Mula'i, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They distracted us from the middle prayer, the 'Asr prayer; may Allah fill their bellies and their graves with fire."
"21392","This is what the women transmitted with isnad from Umm Salamah. Zaynab bint Umm Salamah from Umm Salamah. Hisham ibn 'Urwah from his father from Zaynab. 794 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to me, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that Zaynab bint Umm Salamah narrated to him, from Umm Salamah, she said: Umm Sulaym entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, is ghusl incumbent upon a woman when she has a wet dream? He said: Yes, when she sees water."
"21393","795 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from Zaynab, from Umm Salamah, the same."
"21394","796 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that she said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do I have reward for spending on the children of Abu Salamah, for I spend on them and I do not leave them to fend for themselves? He said: Yes, you have the reward of what you spent on them."
"21395","797 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while an effeminate man was with me, and he heard him saying to Abdullah ibn Abi Umayyah: O Abdullah, if Allah grants you conquest of al-Ta'if tomorrow, then take the daughter of Ghaylan, for she comes forward with four and turns away with eight. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These shall not enter upon you."
"21396","798 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from Zaynab, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am only a human being, and you bring disputes to me, and perhaps one of you is more eloquent in his plea than another, so I judge for him according to what I hear. So whoever I judge for him anything of his brother's right, let him not take anything of it, for I only cut for him a piece of the Fire."
"21397","799 - Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded her to meet him on the Day of Sacrifice at Makkah."
"21398","800 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, both said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded charity, so Zaynab, the wife of Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, said: Will it suffice me of charity that I give charity to my husband while he is poor, and to sons of a brother of mine who are orphans, while I am spending on them in any case? He said: Yes. And she was skilled with her hands."
"21399","Al-Zuhri from 'Urwah. 801 - Al-Firyabi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Khaba'iri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from Zaynab, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a slave girl with a dark mark on her face, and he said: Seek ruqyah for her, for she is afflicted by the evil eye."
"21400","Abu al-Zinad Abdullah ibn Dhakwan from 'Urwah, from Zaynab. 802 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from 'Urwah, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: Umm Sulaym entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, is ghusl incumbent upon a woman when she has a wet dream? He said: Yes, when she sees water."
"21401","803 - Ali narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from 'Urwah, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am only a human being, and you bring disputes to me, and perhaps one of you is more eloquent in his plea than another, so I judge for him according to what I hear. So whoever I judge for him anything of his brother's right, let him not take anything of it, for I only cut for him a piece of the Fire."
"21402","Abu al-Aswad from 'Urwah, from Zaynab. 804 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Malik informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: I complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that I was ill, so he said: Circumambulate behind the people while riding. She said: So I circumambulated, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with the people beside the House, reciting al-Tur: By the Book inscribed."
"21403","805 - Abu al-Zinba' narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Maymun ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Makhramah ibn Bukayr, from his father, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman say: I heard 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr say: I heard Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: I performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I complained before circumambulating the House. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ride and circumambulate riding behind the people, while he was then praying at the edge of the House."
"21404","Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Zaynab. 806 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, 'Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Abu Bakr ibn al-Mundhir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissed while fasting."
"21405","807 - Ahmad ibn Dawud narrated to us, al-Hawdi narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, 'Uthman narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Ulayyah narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that she and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bathe from one vessel from janabah."
"21406","808 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bakr Abu Ja'far al-Siraj al-'Askari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, 'Anbasah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ya'qub, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Zaynab bint Umm Salamah narrated to him, that Umm Salamah narrated to her, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting."
"21407","809 - Husayn narrated to us, 'Uthman narrated to us, Ibn 'Ulayyah narrated to us, from Hisham, from Yahya, with its isnad, similar to it."
"21408","810 - Ahmad ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Husayn al-Mu'allim, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Zaynab, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and she used to bathe from one vessel."
"21409","811 - Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Bishr narrated to us, Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, that Zaynab bint Abi Salamah informed him, from Umm Salamah, that a woman of Aslam called Subay'ah was under her husband and he died leaving her pregnant. Then Abu al-Sanabil ibn Ba'kak proposed to her, but she refused to marry him. He said: It is not lawful for you to marry until you complete the longer of the two terms. She waited twenty nights, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to her: Marry."
"21410","Humayd ibn Nafi' from Zaynab from Umm Salamah. 812 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us. And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both said: al-Qa'nabi narrated to us. And Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, they said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Humayd ibn Nafi', that Zaynab bint Abi Salamah informed him, she said: I heard Umm Salamah say: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my daughter's husband has died and her eyes have complained; may I apply kohl to her? He said: No, two or three times, each time saying: No. Then he said: It is only four months and ten days, while one of you used to throw a dung at the head of the year."
"21411","813 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, 'Asim narrated to us, Shu'bah ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Nafi', he said: I heard Zaynab bint Umm Salamah narrate, from her mother, that a woman whose husband died and whose eye complained came, so they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sought his permission for kohl, mentioning that they feared for her eye. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One of you used to remain in her house a year, then when a year passed she threw a dung; will you not observe four months and ten days?"
"21412","814 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu 'Ubayd al-Qasim ibn Sallam narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from 'Asim ibn Sulayman, from Hafsah bint Sirin, she said: Humayd ibn Nafi' wrote to Humayd al-Himyari and mentioned the hadith of Zaynab bint Abi Salamah. Shu'bah said: So I said to 'Asim: I have heard it from Humayd. He said: You? I said: Yes. He said: And 'Asim thought that he had died a hundred years ago. None transmitted it from Shu'bah except Hajjaj, and none transmitted it from him except Abu 'Ubayd and Ahmad ibn Hanbal."
"21413","815 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, 'Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us. And he said: And Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed me, from Humayd ibn Nafi', from Zaynab, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to the hadith of Shu'bah from Humayd ibn Nafi'."
"21414","816 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Abi 'Umar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Humayd ibn Nafi', from Zaynab, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"21415","817 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed me, from Humayd ibn Nafi', from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, that she heard Umm Habibah and Umm Salamah mention that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that a daughter of hers whose husband died complained of her eyes and she wished to apply kohl to her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One of you used to throw a dung at the head of the year, while it is only four months and ten days."
"21416","Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Zaynab. 818 - Al-Hasan ibn Ghulayb al-Misri narrated to us, 'Imran ibn Harun al-Ramli narrated to us. And Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Hamdani narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah informed me, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrate, from Zaynab, that Umm Salamah informed her, that the daughter of Nu'aym ibn Abdullah al-'Adawi came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My daughter's husband has died, and she was under al-Mughirah al-Makhzumi, and she is in mourning and complains of her eyes; may she apply kohl? He said: No. Then she was silent a while, then said: She complains of her eyes beyond what we think; may she apply kohl? He said: No. Then he said: It is not lawful for a Muslim woman to mourn more than three days except for a husband, four months and ten days."
"21417","Abu Qilabah Abdullah ibn Zayd from Zaynab from Umm Salamah. 819 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us. And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Asad al-'Ammi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Qilabah, from Zaynab, from Umm Salamah, she said: My bedding was opposite the prayer place of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"21418","820 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed me, from Khalid, from Abu Qilabah, from Zaynab, from Umm Salamah, she said: My bedding was opposite the prayer place of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"21419","821 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, both said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Qilabah, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray upon a khumrah."
"21420","822 - Ahmad ibn Mas'ud al-Maqdisi narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn al-Sari ibn Mihran narrated to us, Bashshar ibn Musa narrated to us, both said: Sharik narrated to us, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Qilabah, from Zaynab, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray upon a mat."
"21421","Ali ibn al-Husayn from Zaynab from Umm Salamah. 823 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Asbahani narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He was presented a shoulder, then prayed without performing ablution."
"21422","824 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, from Zaynab, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a sheep's shoulder and ate of it, then prayed without touching water."
"21423","'Asim, freedman of Banu Jumah, from Zaynab from Umm Salamah. 825 - Abu Yahya al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, Junadah narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, from 'Asim, freedman of Banu Jumah, from Umm Salamah, or from Zaynab, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to supplicate and say: O Allah, You are the First, nothing before You, and You are the Last, nothing after You; I seek refuge in You from the evil of every creature whose forelock is in Your Hand, and I seek refuge in You from sin and laziness, and from the punishment of the Fire and the punishment of the grave, and from the trial of wealth and the trial of poverty, and I seek refuge in You from sinfulness and debt; O Allah, purify my heart of sinfulness as the white garment is purified of filth, and distance me from my sin as You distanced between the east and the west."
"21424","Umm Kulthum bint Umm Salamah from Umm Salamah. 826 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us. And al-'Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us. And Abd al-Malik ibn Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us. And Ahmad ibn Sahl al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Kathir ibn Yahya, companion of al-Basri, narrated to us, they said: Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji narrated to us, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from his mother, from Umm Kulthum bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took me in marriage, he said: O Umm Salamah, I have gifted to the Negus musk and a robe, and I do not see him but that he has died, and I do not see my gift but that it will be returned to me. She said: And it was as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said; so he gave his wives an ounce each, and gave me the rest of the musk and the robe."
"21425","827 - Abu Yahya al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, Junadah ibn Salim narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, from his mother, from Umm Kulthum bint Zaynab, from Umm Salamah, that she said: When Abu Salamah died while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with him, I rose intending to weep over him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: What will you do? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I weep over Abu Salamah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not do so, for the family of the deceased have at the death of their deceased whatever they supplicate for."
"21426","828 - Al-Khallal narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Umm Kulthum bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I weep over Abu Salamah? He said: Do not do so, for the family of the deceased have at their deceased whatever they supplicate for."
"21427","829 - Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Umm Kulthum bint Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Asad, from Umm Salamah, she said: When Abu Salamah died, I prepared to weep, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What will you do? I said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Salamah, I weep over him. He said: Do not do so, for the family of the deceased have at their deceased whatever they supplicate for."
"21428","830 - Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Umm Kulthum bint Abdullah ibn Zam'ah, that her grandmother Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), handed her a brass washbasin, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bathe in it. Talhah said: And it was about a sa' or less."
"21429","831 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Hind bint al-Harith, from Umm Salamah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salam, he would remain a little."
"21430","832 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, 'Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Hind bint al-Harith, from Umm Salamah: that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salam, he would remain in his place a short while."
"21431","833 - Ahmad ibn 'Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id and 'Amr ibn Dinar and Ma'mar ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Hind bint al-Harith, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked one night at the sky and said: Glory be to Allah, what trials have been sent down tonight? Or what treasuries have been opened? Wake the mistresses of the chambers, for many a clothed one in this world will be naked on the Day of Resurrection."
"21432","834 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Hind bint al-Harith, from Umm Salamah, she said: Women used to attend the dawn prayer with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then leave wrapped in their woolen garments, unrecognized in the darkness."
"21433","Hind bint al-Harith from Umm Salamah. 835 - Al-Khallal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi 'Umar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from al-Zuhri, from Hind bint al-Harith, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one night: Glory be to Allah, what trials have been sent down? What treasuries have been opened? Wake the mistresses of the chambers, for many a clothed one in this world will be naked on the Day of Resurrection."
"21434","836 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Hind bint al-Harith, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) awoke one night saying: There is no god but Allah, what treasuries have been opened tonight? There is no god but Allah, what trial has been sent down tonight? Who will wake the mistresses of the chamber? O many a clothed one in this world naked in the Hereafter."
"21435","Safiyyah bint Shaybah from Umm Salamah. 837 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed me, from Ibn Khaytham, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Umm Salamah, she said: When the emigrants came to Madinah, they wished to approach women from behind in their front passages, and they disapproved of that. So they came to Umm Salamah and mentioned that to her, so she asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Your women are a tillage for you, so come to your tillage as you wish, one opening only."
"21436","838 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, both said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Ma'mar informed me, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim ibn Yannaq, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The widow whose husband has died shall not dye, nor apply kohl, nor perfume herself, nor wear a dyed garment, nor wear jewelry."
"21437","Umm Habibah bint Kaysan from Umm Salamah. 839 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Hisham al-Harrani narrated to us, 'Uthman narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muslim al-Hashimi, from Umm Habibah bint Kaysan, from Umm Salamah, she said: This verse was revealed: Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the House, while I was in my house. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called al-Hasan and al-Husayn, seating one upon his right thigh and the other upon his left thigh, and Fatimah cast a cloak over them. When: Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the House was revealed, I said: Am I with you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: And you are with us."
"21438","What Safiyyah bint Abi 'Ubayd transmitted from Umm Salamah. 840 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Nafi', from Safiyyah, from Umm Salamah, she said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about women's trains, and he said: A handspan. I said: Then their feet will show? He said: Then an arm's length."
"21439","841 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Iqal al-Harrani narrated to us, al-Nufayli narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Hisham al-Harrani narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Nafi', from Safiyyah bint Abi 'Ubayd, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever drinks from a vessel of gold or silver only gurgles in his belly the fire of Hell."
"21440","842 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Nafi', from Safiyyah bint Abi 'Ubayd, from 'A'ishah and Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead one more than three, except over her husband."
"21441","843 - Al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, 'Ayyash al-Raqqam narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Nafi', from Safiyyah bint Abi 'Ubayd, from Umm Salamah and 'A'ishah, that they heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead one more than three, except over her husband."
"21442","844 - Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Siraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to me, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Safiyyah bint Abi 'Ubayd, from Umm Salamah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The one who drinks from a silver vessel only gurgles in his belly the fire of Hell."
"21443","The umm walad of Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf from Umm Salamah. 845 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Muhammad ibn 'Umarah ibn Hazm, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, from an umm walad of Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, from Umm Salamah, that she asked her, saying: I am a woman who lengthens my train and walks in filthy places. Umm Salamah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What comes after it purifies it."
"21444","846 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Umarah al-Taymi, from the umm walad of Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"21445","'Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman from Umm Salamah. 847 - Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us. And 'Abdan ibn Ahmad and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, both said: Zakariya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, both said: Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from 'Amrah, from Umm Salamah, she said: We had a sheep we milked, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed it and said: What happened to your sheep? They said: It died. He said: What did you do with its hide? They said: O Messenger of Allah, we threw it away. He said: Why did you not benefit from it? For its tanning is its purification, lawful as vinegar from wine is lawful."
"21446","848 - Abd al-Malik ibn Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from 'Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: There was noise in the chamber of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he came out wrapped in his cloak, and said: Who are these? They said: They are disputing, O Messenger of Allah. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged between them, then said: I judge between you, and perhaps one of you is more eloquent than his brother in speech, so I judge for him according to what is clear to me; so whoever I judge for him anything that is not his, I only give him his portion of the Fire."
"21447","Hukaymah from Umm Salamah. 849 - Abd al-Malik ibn Yahya narrated to us, my father narrated to us. And al-Husayn narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, both said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Uthman, from Yahya ibn Abi Sufyan, from his grandmother Hukaymah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever enters ihram from Bayt al-Maqdis, his past sins are forgiven."
"21448","Rumaythah from Umm Salamah. 850 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from 'Awf ibn al-Harith, from Rumaythah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Umm Salamah, do not hurt me concerning 'A'ishah, for revelation never came down upon me while any of my wives was with me except 'A'ishah; revelation came down upon me while she was with me in my blanket."
"21449","Umm Muhammad ibn Qays from Umm Salamah. 851 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, both said: Waki' narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Muhammad ibn Bakr, from his father, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the chamber of Umm Salamah, when her son 'Umar or Abdullah passed in front of him, so he motioned with his hand thus, and he returned. Then Zaynab passed, so he motioned with his hand thus, but she went on. He said: They are predominant."
"21450","And among the women of the people of Basrah from Umm Salamah. Umm al-Hasan from Umm Salamah; al-Hasan from his mother. 852 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar, and 'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, they said: 'Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning 'Ammar: The rebellious party will kill him."
"21451","853 - Ibrahim ibn Salih narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas narrated to us, Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated to us, both said: 'Awf narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning 'Ammar: The rebellious party will kill him."
"21452","854 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu 'Ubayd narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh informed me, he said: Ibn 'Awn narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: I have not forgotten the trace at his chest on the Day of the Trench, while he handed them milk, saying: O Allah, the true good is the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirah. When he saw him, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: O son of Sumayyah, the rebellious party will kill you."
"21453","855 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Ulayyah narrated to us, from Ibn 'Awn, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The rebellious party will kill 'Ammar."
"21454","856 - 'Umar ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Sahl al-Sarraj, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The rebellious party will kill 'Ammar."
"21455","857 - 'Abdan ibn Ahmad and Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Yunus ibn 'Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The rebellious party will kill 'Ammar."
"21456","858 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Fadl ibn Dawud al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Awf, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"21457","859 - Al-Saji narrated to us, Bundar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Musa al-Mar'i, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rak'ahs sitting after witr."
"21458","860 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Najiyah and Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Sarraj narrated to us, both said: Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, 'Anbasah narrated to us, from Zakariya ibn Hakim, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rak'ahs sitting after his witr."
"21459","861 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from my grandfather. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan al-'Allaf narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) awoke from his sleep uttering istirja', so I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the matter with you? He said: A party of my ummah will be swallowed up, then resurrected toward a man; he will come to Makkah, and he will prevent him, and they will be swallowed up; their place of perishing is one, but their sources are diverse; among them is one who is coerced and comes coerced."
"21460","862 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Makhram Abu Qatadah al-Basri narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from 'Amr, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: Indeed We have granted you al-Kawthar."
"21461","863 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jumhur ibn Mansur narrated to us, Sinan ibn Harun al-Burjumi narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Abd al-Malik, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - used to perform ablution with a mudd and take the ritual bath with a sa'."
"21462","864 - Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would keep away because of the onset of bleeding for three, then he would resume marital intimacy after the three."
"21463","865 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla and Abdan both narrated to us, they said: Hisham ibn Khalid narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Salim al-Khayyat narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan narrating, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would often say: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, how often you supplicate with this supplication! He said: O Umm Salamah, the heart of the son of Adam is between two fingers of the fingers of the Lord of the worlds; if He wills He keeps it upright, and if He wills He turns it astray."
"21464","866 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim and al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Raziyan narrated to us, they said: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, (ha). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, they both said: Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: The urine of a boy is sprinkled over, and the urine of a girl is washed."
"21465","867 - Ahmad ibn Sahl al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Muqri narrated to us, Salim ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: I used to rub semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"21466","868 - Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Jarud and Salm ibn Isam narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Hafs ibn Hisham ibn Zayd ibn Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Nuh al-Attar narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: I and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - used to bathe from a single vessel, and I would say to him: Leave some for me, leave some for me."
"21467","869 - Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated to us, Abu Hammam al-Khariji narrated to us, Adi ibn Abi Adi narrated to me, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: In every rak'ah there is a tashahhud and taslim upon the Messengers, and upon those who followed them among the righteous servants of Allah."
"21468","870 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Amr ibn Hashim al-Bayruti narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abi Karimah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me about the saying of Allah: And houris with wide eyes. He said: Hur means white, and in means those with large eyes. I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me about His saying: As if they were sheltered pearls. He said: Their purity is like the purity of pearls in shells untouched by hands. I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me about His saying: In them are good and beautiful women. He said: Good in character, beautiful in faces. I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me about His saying: As if they were sheltered eggs. He said: Their delicacy is like the delicacy of the skin you see inside the egg next to the shell. I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me about His saying: Devoted and of equal age. He said: They are those who died in this world as aged, gray-haired old women; Allah created them anew after old age and made them virgins, loving, beloved, of equal age, born at one time. I said: O Messenger of Allah, are the women of this world superior, or the wide-eyed houris? He said: Rather the women of this world are superior to the wide-eyed houris, like the superiority of the outer garment over the lining. I said: O Messenger of Allah, for what reason? He said: Because of their prayer, their fasting, and their worship of Allah. Allah clothed their faces with light and their bodies with silk: white in complexion, green in dress, yellow in adornment, their censers are pearls and their combs are gold. They say: We are the eternal ones who never die, and we are the blissful ones who never suffer, and we are the residents who never depart, and we are the content ones who never become angry. Glad tidings to the one we belong to and who belongs to us. I said: O Messenger of Allah, a woman among us marries two, three, or four husbands, then dies and enters Paradise, and they enter with her - which of them will be her husband? He said: O Umm Salamah, she will be given the choice and will choose the best of them in character, and she will say: O my Lord, this one had the best character with me in this world, so marry me to him. O Umm Salamah, good character has taken away the good of this world and the Hereafter."
"21469","871 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Rashid al-Adami narrated to us, Abu Rabi'ah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd and Humayd, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - measured out a span of the hem for Fatimah."
"21470","872 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Amr ibn Makhram Abu Qatadah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Act and do not rely on hope alone, for my intercession is for the ruined ones of my ummah."
"21471","Sa'id ibn Abi al-Hasan from his mother from Umm Salamah. 873 - Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Sa'id ibn Abi al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Ammar will be killed by the rebellious faction."
"21472","874 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Sa'id ibn Abi al-Hasan, he said: Our mother narrated to us, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to Ammar: The rebellious faction will kill him."
"21473","875 - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Jawhari narrated to us, Qahtabah ibn Ghudanah narrated to us, Abu Umayyah ibn Ya'la narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - he said: Whoever says in the morning: Praise be to Allah, before whose majesty everything humbles itself, ten good deeds are written for him."
"21474","876 - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Qahtabah ibn Ghudanah narrated to us, Abu Umayyah narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - when he went out to prayer would say: O Allah, make me the closest of those who draw near to You, and the most honored of those who turn to You, and the most persistent of those who ask You."
"21475","877 - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Qahtabah ibn Ghudanah narrated to us, Abu Umayyah ibn Ya'la narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever says every day: O Allah, forgive me and the believing men and believing women, a good deed is added for him for every believer."
"21476","Mussah from Umm Salamah. 878 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, (ha). And Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Ali ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Abu Sahl of the people of Basrah, from Mussah, from Umm Salamah, she said: Women at the time of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would sit after their postnatal bleeding for forty nights, and we would pray with wars covering our faces because of melasma."
"21477","Kabshah bint Abi Maryam from Umm Salamah. 879 - Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Thabit ibn Umarah narrated to us, from Raytah, from Kabshah bint Abi Maryam, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would forbid mixing dates with raisins, and cooking date-stones into a thick brew."
"21478","880 - al-Judhu'i narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, (ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, Raytah bint Hurayth narrated to me, from Kabshah bint Abi Maryam, that she asked Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - about drinks, and she said: I inform you of what the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - used to forbid his family: he used to forbid us to mix raisins with dates."
"21479","And among the women of the people of Kufah: Amrah bint Af'a from Umm Salamah. 881 - al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Dallal at Kufah narrated to us, Mukhawwal ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Amrah bint Af'a, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: No one should be in a state of janabah in this mosque except me and Ali."
"21480","Salma from Umm Salamah. 882 - Ali ibn al-Abbas al-Bajali narrated to us, Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, Razin narrated to me, Salma narrated to me, she said: I entered upon Umm Salamah while she was weeping, and I said: What makes you weep? She said: I saw the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - meaning in a dream - with dust on his head and beard, and I said: What is wrong with you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I just witnessed the killing of al-Husayn."
"21481","Jasrah from Umm Salamah. 883 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Ibn Abi Utbah narrated to us, from Abu al-Khattab al-Hajari, from Mahduj al-Dhuhli, from Jasrah, she said: Umm Salamah informed me, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - went out to the mosque and called out at the top of his voice: This mosque is not lawful for one in janabah nor for a menstruating woman, except for the Prophet and his wives and Fatimah bint Muhammad, and Ali. I have made it clear to you so that you do not go astray."
"21482","Umm Musawir al-Himyari from Umm Salamah. 884 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (ha). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Isma'il al-Talqani narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Musawir al-Himyari, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: Any woman who dies while her husband is pleased with her will enter Paradise."
"21483","885 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (ha). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Isma'il al-Talqani narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Abu Nasr Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Musawir al-Himyari, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: No believer hates Ali, and no hypocrite loves him."
"21484","886 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Wasil narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu Nasr, from Musawir al-Himyari, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would say: None loves Ali except a believer, and none hates him except a hypocrite."
"21485","Umm Musa from Umm Salamah. 887 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman narrated to us, they said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Umm Musa, from Umm Salamah, she said: By the One by whom Umm Salamah swears, the closest of people to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - was Ali. We were with the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - in the house of A'ishah, and I was the last to leave the house; then we sat nearest to the door, and Ali leaned over him, so he was the last of people to be in his company, conversing with him privately."
"21486","The grandmother of Ibn Jud'an from Umm Salamah. 888 - Abu Yahya al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, (ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Waki' narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Abd Allah, from Ibn Jud'an, from his grandmother, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: There is no alliance in Islam, and no alliance of the pre-Islamic period but Islam only strengthened it."
"21487","889 - Abu Yahya narrated to us, Sahl narrated to us, (ha). And al-Husayn narrated to us, Uthman narrated to us, (ha). And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Waki' narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Abd Allah, from Ibn Jud'an, from his grandmother, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - called a maidservant of his and she was slow to come to him, so he said: Were it not for fear of retribution on the Day of Resurrection, I would have hurt you with this siwak."
"21488","890 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman narrated to us, (ha). And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Waki' narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Abd Allah, from Ibn Jud'an, from his grandmother, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: The one consulted is entrusted."
"21489","Umm Mubashshir from Umm Salamah. 891 - Abu Yahya al-Razi narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Salim ibn Talhah narrated to us, Jami' ibn Abi Rashid narrated to us while his tears were flowing down, from Umm Mubashshir, from Umm Salamah, that she heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: When evil appears in the land, Allah sends down His punishment upon the people of the land. I said: O Messenger of Allah, even if there are righteous people among them? He said: Yes, even if there are righteous people among them, what befalls the people befalls them, then they return to the mercy and forgiveness of Allah."
"21490","Additions in the hadith of Umm Salamah. Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas from Umm Salamah. 892 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Aban narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from his father, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to Ali: Are you not pleased to be to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me?"
"21491","Umar ibn Abi Salamah from Umm Salamah. 893 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - while she was ill, and he said to her: Will you not go out with us on this journey of ours? She said: O Messenger of Allah, I am ill and I fear my illness will detain me. He said: Then enter ihram for Hajj and say: O Allah, my place of release is where You detain me."
"21492","894 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb al-Simsar narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Abd Rabbihi ibn Sa'id, from Abdullah ibn Ka'b al-Himyari, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - similar to it."
"21493","Ibn Abbas from Umm Salamah. 895 - Ya'qub ibn Ishaq ibn al-Zubayr al-Halabi narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would pray witr with seven or five, without separating between them with a taslim or speech."
"21494","Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i from Umm Salamah. 896 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Tara'ifi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Maymun al-Raqqi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: The one who is affectionate toward you after me is the truthful, dutiful one. O Allah, give Ibn Awf to drink from the Salsabil of Paradise."
"21495","Safina, the freedman of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah. 897 - Zakariyya ibn Hamdawayh al-Saffar narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Safinah, the freedman of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would say during the illness in which he died: Prayer, and what your right hands possess. He kept saying it until his tongue could no longer utter it."
"21496","898 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Salim ibn Abdullah informed me that Safinah, the freedman of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - informed him, that Umm Salamah informed him, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell."
"21497","899 - Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu al-Nadr Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, al-Zubaydi narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn Abdullah, that Safinah, the freedman of Umm Salamah, informed him, that Umm Salamah said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell."
"21498","Amir ibn Abi Umayyah from Umm Salamah. 900 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Amir ibn Abi Umayyah, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would wake up in janabah and then fast."
"21499","Abu al-Tufayl from Umm Salamah. 901 - Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Awf al-Himsi narrated to us, Abu Jabir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Muhammad, an old Makkan shaykh, narrated to us, from Fitr ibn Khalifah, from Abu al-Tufayl, he said: I heard Umm Salamah say: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: Whoever loves Ali has loved me, and whoever loves me has loved Allah; and whoever hates Ali has hated me, and whoever hates me has hated Allah."
"21500","al-Zuhri from Urwah from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah from Umm Salamah. 902 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed me, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: Zaynab bint Umm Salamah narrated to me, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - heard the noise of a dispute at the door of Umm Salamah, so he went out to them and said: You dispute before me, but I am only a human being; perhaps one of you is more eloquent in his plea than the other, so I judge for him based on what I hear, thinking him truthful. So whoever I judge for him something of the right of his brother, it is a piece of the Fire - let him take it or leave it."
"21501","903 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Musa al-Taymi narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, that Zaynab bint Umm Salamah informed him, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - heard the clamor of disputants at the door of Umm Salamah, so he went out to them and mentioned similar to it."
"21502","Hisham ibn Urwah from his father from Zaynab. 904 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that Umm Habibah said: O Messenger of Allah, would you like to marry my sister, the daughter of Abu Sufyan? He said: No, she is not lawful for me. She said: I heard that you are proposing Durrah bint Abi Salamah. He said: The daughter of Umm Salamah - by Allah, even if she were not my stepdaughter under my care, she would not be lawful for me; she is the daughter of my brother through nursing: Thuwaybah nursed me and her. So do not offer me your sisters or your daughters."
"21503","905 - Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Zaynab, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - similar to it."
"21504","906 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: You dispute before me, but I am only a human being; perhaps one of you is more eloquent in his plea than the other, so I only judge between you according to what I hear from you. Whoever I judge for him something of the right of his brother, let him not take it, for I am only cutting for him a piece of the fire of Hell which he will bring on the Day of Resurrection."
"21505","907 - Mus'ab al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Zaynab, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - similar to it."
"21506","908 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Zaynab, from Umm Salamah, she said: Umm Sulaym came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and asked him about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. He said: If she sees water, let her bathe. I said to her: You have shamed women - does a woman have a wet dream? The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: May your right hand be dusted - how else would her son resemble her?"
"21507","909 - Mus'ab narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Zaynab, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - similar to it."
"21508","910 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered upon her and heard an effeminate man saying to Abdullah ibn Abi Umayyah: If Allah conquers al-Ta'if tomorrow, I will show you a woman who comes forward with four and goes back with eight. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Expel them from your houses."
"21509","911 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, the sons of Abu Salamah are under my care and they have nothing except what I spend - will I have a reward if I spend on them? The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Spend on them, and you will have the reward of what you spend on them."
"21510","Abu Salamah from Zaynab. 912 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: While I was lying with the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - in a blanket, I menstruated."
"21511","913 - al-Judhu'i narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Salim ibn Nuh narrated to us, from Umar ibn Amir, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Zaynab, from Umm Salamah, she said: I and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and she mentioned similar to it."
"21512","914 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Zaynab, from Umm Salamah, that she used to bathe with the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - from a single vessel for janabah, and that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would kiss her while he was fasting."
"21513","Nafi', the freedman of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah. 915 - Hajjaj ibn Imran al-Sadusi narrated to us, Abu Salamah Yahya ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Abd Rabbihi, from Abu Iyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, that Marwan ibn al-Hakam sent him to Umm Salamah; he said: I met her slave Nafi', so he sent him to her and he asked her, then he returned to him and informed him that she narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would wake up in janabah from intercourse, not from a wet dream, then wake up fasting."
"21514","Sulayman ibn Yasar from Umm Salamah. 916 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah and Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Umm Salamah, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what about women? He said: Let them lower a span. I said: Then it will be uncovered from them. He said: Then a cubit, and let them not exceed it."
"21515","917 - Ubayd narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr, Abu Usamah, and Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umayr, from Nafi', from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Umm Salamah, she said: A woman asked the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and said: O Messenger of Allah, I suffer istihadah and do not become pure - shall I leave prayer? He said: No, but leave the number of days and nights you used to menstruate, and their measure of the month, then bathe, pad yourself, and pray."
"21516","918 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Malik informed me, from Nafi', from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Umm Salamah, that a woman suffered heavy bleeding at the time of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - so Umm Salamah asked the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - about that for her, and he said: Let her consider the number of nights and days she used to menstruate and their measure, and let her leave prayer; then when she has passed that, let her bathe, pad herself with a cloth, and pray."
"21517","919 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - the hadith."
"21518","920 - Mus'ab narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi', that Sulayman ibn Yasar informed him, from Umm Salamah, that a woman suffered heavy bleeding at the time of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - so Umm Salamah asked the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - for her, and the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Let her consider the number of days and nights she used to menstruate before this befell her, and their measure of the month, and leave prayer for that; then when she has passed that and prayer time comes, let her bathe and pray."
"21519","Abdullah ibn Rafi' from Umm Salamah. 921 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Abdullah ibn Rafi', from Umm Salamah, she said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would wake up in janabah without a wet dream, then bathe and continue his fast."
"21520","922 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Muhammad ibn Yusuf, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Umm Salamah, she said: I brought near to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - a roasted side, and he ate from it, then stood for prayer without performing ablution."
"21521","Ata ibn Yasar from Umm Salamah. 923 - Wathilah ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Kathir ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Ayyash, Abu Bakr al-Tamimi narrated to me, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever is tried with judging between Muslims, let him be equal between them in seating, gesture, and look, and let him not raise his voice toward one disputant more than the other."
"21522","Abu Salamah from Umm Salamah. 924 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Tahla, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would perform ablution because of what fire touched."
"21523","Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman from Umm Salamah. 925 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Makhramah informed me, from his father, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Muslim say: I heard Muhammad ibn Muslim the hadith, (ha). And Muhammad ibn Salih al-Narsi narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Umar, from Amr ibn Muslim, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - he said: Whoever enters Dhul-Hijjah and has a sacrifice he wants to slaughter, let him refrain from his hair and nails."
"21524","Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Umm Salamah. 926 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Yazid ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: The one who eats or drinks in vessels of silver and gold only drags fire of Hell in his belly."
"21525","927 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Malik informed me, (ha). And Mus'ab al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, (ha). And al-Shafi'i narrated to us, he said: My uncle narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, all of them: from Nafi', from Zayd ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - similar to it."
"21526","928 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my uncle narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, Nafi' informed me that Zayd ibn Abdullah informed him, that Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr informed him, that Umm Salamah informed him, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: The one who drinks in a silver vessel only drags fire of Hell in his belly, unless he repents."
"21527","Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal from Umm Salamah. 929 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, he said: Mu'awiyah sent to Umm Salamah, so she went with the messenger, and he asked Umm Salamah, and she said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - forbade them, meaning the two rak'ahs after Asr. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - while performing ablution for Zuhr - and he had sent a collector, and the Muhajirun were with him, and their affair concerned him - when the door was knocked, he went out and prayed Zuhr, then came and distributed what was brought, and remained so until he prayed Asr, then entered his house and prayed two rak'ahs, then said: The affair of the collector kept me from praying them after Zuhr, so I prayed them after Asr."
"21528","930 - Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Allegiance will be pledged to a man between the Corner and the Station, with the number of the people of Badr; the groups of the people of Iraq and the abdals of Sham will come to him, and an army from Sham will raid them until, when they are at al-Bayda, they will be swallowed up; then a man of Quraysh whose maternal uncles are Kalb will raid them, and they will meet and Allah will defeat them. It used to be said: The loser is the one who loses the spoils of Kalb."
"21529","Mujahid from Umm Salamah. 931 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Mujahid, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: There will be disagreement at the death of a caliph, and a man of Banu Hashim will go out from Madinah to Makkah; people will come to him and pledge allegiance to him between the Corner and the Station, while he dislikes it. An army from Sham will be prepared against them until, when they are at al-Bayda, they will be swallowed up. The groups of the people of Iraq and the abdals of Sham will come to them, and a man in Sham whose maternal uncles are Kalb will rise and prepare an army against them, and Allah will defeat them, and the turn will be against them. That is the day of Kalb, and the loser is the one who loses the spoils of Kalb. He will extract treasures, distribute wealth, and Islam will cast its reins to the earth; he will live so for seven years or six years. Ubayd Allah said: I narrated it to Layth, and he said: Mujahid narrated it to me."
"21530","932 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Shayban, from Mansur, from Mujahid, that Umm Salamah said: O Messenger of Allah, Hisham ibn al-Mughirah used to feed food, honor guests, uphold kinship, and free captives - had he lived to meet you he would have become Muslim - will he have reward for that? He said: He was your uncle; he gave for this world, its mention and its beauty, and he never once said: Forgive me on the Day of Judgment."
"21531","933 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, al-Minhal ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Salamah, from Mujahid, from Umm Salamah, she said: One of us would menstruate and have only a single garment, while today one of us empties her servant to wash her clothes to purify them."
"21532","934 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, he said: Umm Salamah was asked: Does a woman cover her face while in ihram? She said: Riders used to pass by us while we were with the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and one of us would lower the garment over her face."
"21533","Ubayd ibn Umayr from Umm Salamah. 935 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Isa ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Umm Salamah, she said: I and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would bathe from a single vessel, each of us taking separately."
"21534","936 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Khashshab al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abu Sa'd al-Ansari, from a man of the people of Madinah, from Umm Salamah, she said: I was with the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and menstruation came upon me, so I left the bed, and the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Wrap your waist-wrapper and return."
"21535","Ibn Abi Mulaykah from Umm Salamah. 937 - Ubayd narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would recite: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds - letter by letter."
"21536","al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab from Umm Salamah. 938 - Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever spends on two daughters or two sisters or two female relatives, seeking reward for the spending on them until Allah suffices them and enriches them from His bounty, they will be a screen for him from the Fire."
"21537","Abu Atiyyah al-Tufawi from Umm Salamah. 939 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu Zafar narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Mutahhar narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Awf, (ha). And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Atiyyah Abu al-Mu'addil al-Tufawi, from his father, he said: Umm Salamah informed me that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - was with her in her house one day when the servant came and said: Ali and Fatimah are at the doorstep. He said: Step aside from my household. So I stepped aside to a corner of the house, and Ali, Fatimah, Hasan, and Husayn came, the two of them small boys. He took Hasan and Husayn and placed them in his lap, took Ali with one of his hands and embraced him, and covered them with a black cloak, then said: O Allah, to You, not to the Fire - me and my household. She said: I called to him and said: And me, O Messenger of Allah? He said: And you."
"21538","Abu Wa'il from Umm Salamah. 940 - Ubayd narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Shaqiq, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: When you attend the sick or the dead, say good, for the angels say amen to what you say. She said: When Abu Salamah died, I came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Salamah has died. He said: Say: O Allah, forgive me and him, and grant me a good successor from him. So I did, and Allah granted me one better than him: Muhammad - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"21539","941 - Ubayd narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Shaqiq, from Umm Salamah, she said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf entered upon her and said: O mother, I fear my abundant wealth will destroy me - I am the wealthiest of Quraysh. She said: O my son, give charity, for I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: Among my companions are those who will not see me after I die. So Abd al-Rahman went out and met Umar, and informed him of what Umm Salamah said. Umar came and entered upon her and said: Am I among them? She said: No, and I will not say that to anyone after you."
"21540","Zadhan from Umm Salamah. 942 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn Muslim al-Sarraj, from Maymun ibn Abi Maymun, from Zadhan, he said: Umm Salamah saw a cousin of hers prostrating, and she said: Dust your face, for the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to a freedman of ours called Rabah, whom he saw prostrating: Dust your face, O Rabah."
"21541","Abu al-Aliyah from Umm Salamah. 943 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far al-Razi, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Umm Salamah, she said: I heard the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - recite: Yes, My signs came to you, but you denied them and were arrogant."
"21542","Abdullah ibn al-Hasan from Umm Salamah. 944 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Hasan, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever does not have one of three in him, let him not reckon anything of his deed: God-consciousness restraining him from disobedience to Allah, or forbearance with which he restrains a fool, or character with which he lives among people."
"21543","945 - And that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever has one of three in him, Allah will marry him to the wide-eyed houris: one who has a hidden, desirable trust and delivers it out of fear of Allah, or a man who pardons his killer, or a man who recites: Say, He is Allah, the One, after every prayer."
"21544","Malik ibn Ja'wanah from Umm Salamah. 946 - al-Asfati narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Ali ibn Ghurab narrated to us, from Musa ibn Qays al-Hadrami, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Iyad, from Malik ibn Ja'wanah: I heard Umm Salamah say: Ali is upon the truth; whoever follows him follows the truth, and whoever leaves him leaves the truth - a covenant made before his death."
"21545","Shahr ibn Hawshab from Umm Salamah. 947 - Allan ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Dinar narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Nashit narrated to us, he said: I heard Shahr ibn Hawshab say: I came to Umm Salamah to condole her for al-Husayn, and she said to me from what she narrated to me: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - was in my house one day, and Fatimah came to him with a dish of broth, and he said: Go and bring your husband, or your cousin, and your two sons. So she went and brought Ali, Hasan, and Husayn. They ate from that food, while the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - was on a sleeping mat of ours, with a Khaybari cloak under him. He took the cloak and covered them with it, then raised his hands to the heaven and said: O Allah, these are my kin and my household, so remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly. Umm Salamah said: Am I of your household? He said: You are toward good."
"21546","Abu Sallam al-Habashi from Umm Salamah. 948 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Shaddad Abu Muhammad narrated to us, from Abu Sallam al-Aswad, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - passed by me while I was weeping for Abu Salamah, and said: Shall I not guide you to something better than what you say? Say istirja' and say: O Allah, make my outcome good, mend my calamity, and replace him for me with better than him. So I returned and said what he told me, then I kept saying: Where would I find one like Abu Salamah? She said: And Allah replaced him for me with one better than Abu Salamah: the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"21547","Abdullah ibn Wahb ibn Zam'ah from Umm Salamah. 949 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Musa ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, my aunt Quraybah bint Abdullah narrated to me, that her father: Umm Salamah said to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: No man revives a land from which a thirsty liver drinks or from which one in good health benefits, except that Allah writes a reward for him for it."
"21548","950 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Shaybani narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Athmah narrated to us, Musa ibn Ya'qub al-Zam'i narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Wahb ibn Zam'ah, that his father informed him, that Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - informed him, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would enter upon his wives every morning and greet them. One of them had honey with her, and whenever he entered upon her she would bring some of it for him, so he would stay with her for that. A'ishah and Hafsah were jealous of that, so when the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered upon them, they said: We smell maghafir from you. So he left that honey."
"21549","951 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ya'qub al-Zam'i, from his aunt Quraybah bint Abdullah ibn Wahb ibn Zam'ah, from her father, he said: Umm Salamah informed me that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Allah has cursed the briber and the bribed in judgment."
"21550","Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah ibn Zam'ah from Umm Salamah. 952 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Muti' al-Adawi narrated to us, from Rukayh ibn Abi Ubaydah, from his father, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered upon me and said: Why do I see you disheveled? I said: I drank a medicine to warm my stomach. He said: What is it? I said: Shubrum. He said: What have you to do with shubrum? It is hot fire. Upon you is senna and sannut, for in them is a cure for everything except death."
"21551","953 - And from Rukayh ibn Abi Ubaydah, from his father, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would sometimes dye his cloak and waist-wrapper with saffron or wars, then go out in them."
"21552","Miqsam from Umm Salamah. 954 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Zuhayr, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would pray witr with nine or ten, without separating between them with a taslim or speech."
"21553","Nabhan from Umm Salamah. 955 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Nabhan, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - that he said: When one of you has a mukatab who has what to pay, let her veil herself from him."
"21554","956 - Yahya ibn Uthman narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Nafi' informed me, from Ibn Yazid, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Nabhan, from Umm Salamah, she said: I was with the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and Maymunah was with him, when Ibn Umm Kulthum came - the hadith."
"21555","Ibn Safinah from Umm Salamah. 957 - Ubayd narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Sa'id, he said: Umar ibn Kathir ibn Aflah informed me, he said: I heard Ibn Safinah mention that he heard Umm Salamah say: I heard the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: There is no servant struck by a calamity - the hadith, and it is in the Book of Death."
"21556","958 - Ubayd narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Sa'id, from Umar ibn Kathir ibn Aflah, from Ibn Safinah, the freedman of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: There is no servant afflicted with a calamity - the hadith."
"21557","Thabit, the freedman of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah. 959 - Mus'ab narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah ibn Nashit, from Thabit, the freedman of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - returned to her house and prayed in it two rak'ahs after Asr. A'ishah sent to Umm Salamah: What is this prayer the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - prayed in your house? She said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - used to pray two rak'ahs after Zuhr, then a delegation of Banu al-Mustaliq came concerning what their collector al-Walid ibn Uqbah did to them. They kept excusing themselves to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - until the mu'adhdhin came calling him to Asr prayer. He prayed the obligatory prayer, then prayed with me in my house those two rak'ahs, which he had never prayed before or after."
"21558","960 - And from Umm Salamah that it was revealed concerning Banu al-Mustaliq, concerning what their collector al-Walid ibn Uqbah did to them: O you who believe, if a corrupt one comes to you with news, verify it - the verse. She said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - had sent to them to collect their wealth in charity. When they heard of him, a group of riders from them came forward and said: We will go with the messenger of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and carry him. When he heard that, he thought they had set out to kill him, so he returned and said: Banu al-Mustaliq have withheld their charities, O Messenger of Allah. The people came until they arrived at Madinah, then lined up behind the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - in the row. When he finished prayer they left and said: We seek refuge in Allah from the anger of Allah and His Messenger. We heard, O Messenger of Allah, of your messenger whom you sent to collect our wealth, and we were pleased with that and our eyes were comforted by it, and we wanted to meet him and go with the messenger of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. We heard that he returned, and we feared his return was due to anger from Allah and His Messenger. They kept excusing themselves to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - until this verse was revealed."
"21559","961 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Thabit, the freedman of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a small bell."
"21560","Abu al-Sa'ib, the freedman of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah. 962 - Ibn Zughbah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Samh, from Abu al-Sa'ib, the freedman of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say: Any woman who removes her clothes in other than her husband's house, Allah tears His cover from her."
"21561","963 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Hakam al-Bunani, he said: Sulayman, the freedman of Umm Salamah, narrated to me, from Umm Salamah, she said: I and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would bathe from a single vessel, about half a faraq, taking turns bathing together, he beginning before me."
"21562","Kurayb from Umm Salamah. 964 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Asad narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Umar narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Kurayb, he said: Ibn Abbas and some people sent me to Umm Salamah to ask her which days the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - fasted most. She said: Saturday and Sunday are the days he fasted most, and he would say: They are two feast days of the polytheists, and I like to differ from them."
"21563","al-Maqburi from Umm Salamah. 965 - Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim al-Zubayri narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Abu Ma'shar, from al-Maqburi, from Umm Salamah, she said: I and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would bathe from a single vessel, both of us in janabah, until my hand and his hand differed."
"21564","Na'im, the freedman of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah. 966 - Abu al-Zinba' narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Ufayr narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Na'im, the freedman of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - concerning a menstruating woman: She washes what has soiled her garment and does not wash the whole garment."
"21565","Abu Salih from Umm Salamah. 967 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Abu Salih, from Umm Salamah, she said: I wore a necklace with hairs of gold in it, and the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saw me and disliked it and turned away from me, so I removed it. He said: What secures you from Allah putting in its place on the Day of Resurrection hairs of fire?"
"21566","968 - al-Khallal narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Utbah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered upon me while I had hairs of gold on me, and he turned away from me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not look at my adornment? He said: From it I turn away. So I cut it off, and he turned his face toward me."
"21567","969 - al-Khallal narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah, from Ata, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would intend fasting from the night, then wake up and say: Do you have anything? We would say: We have nothing - are you not fasting?"
"21568","Nawfal ibn Musahiq from Umm Salamah. 970 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, he said: al-Mundhir ibn al-Jahm al-Aslami narrated to me, from Nawfal ibn Musahiq, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: The womb is a branch holding to the waist of the Most Merciful, pleading its right to Him. He says: Are you not pleased that I join whoever joins you and cut whoever cuts you? Whoever joins you has joined Me, and whoever cuts you has cut Me."
"21569","Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith from Umm Salamah. 971 - Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Abd Rabbihi ibn Sa'id, from Abdullah ibn Ka'b, that Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to him, that Marwan ibn al-Hakam sent him to Umm Salamah to ask her about a man who wakes up in janabah - does he fast? She said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would wake up in janabah from intercourse, not a wet dream, and would neither break his fast nor make it up."
"21570","972 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Salman al-Qulusi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Aban narrated to us, Umar ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Umm Salamah, that al-Harith ibn Hisham came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - in the year of the Farewell Hajj and said: O Messenger of Allah, I used to uphold kinship, do good to neighbors, shelter orphans, feed guests, and feed the poor - and all this Hisham ibn al-Mughirah used to do. What do you think of him, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Every grave whose owner does not bear witness that there is no god but Allah is a brand of fire. I found my uncle Abu Talib in a deep flood of fire, and Allah brought him out because of his place with me and his kindness to me, and placed him in a shallow part of fire."
"21571","973 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would wake up in janabah without a wet dream, then wake up fasting."
"21572","974 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman, Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Umm Salamah said: When the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - proposed to me, I said to him: I have three traits: I am advanced in age, I am a woman with young children, and I am a very jealous woman. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: As for the children, they are for Allah and His Messenger; as for jealousy, I will supplicate to Allah to remove it from you; and as for age, I am older than you in age. So the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - married her while she was nursing her daughter Zaynab bint Abi Salamah. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would enter and go out without approaching her, and when he entered he would jest with her daughter. Then Ammar ibn Yasir entered and said: Where is this daughter of yours who has kept the household of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - busy? He took her and sought a wet nurse for her. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered and said: Where is Zunab? A woman said: Ammar entered and took her and sought a wet nurse for her. Then the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - consummated with his wife."
"21573","Awf ibn al-Harith from Umm Salamah. 975 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Awf ibn al-Harith, he said: Umm Salamah narrated to me that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Do not hurt me concerning A'ishah, for revelation has not descended upon me in the blanket of any one of you other than A'ishah."
"21574","976 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Awf ibn al-Harith, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Do not hurt me concerning A'ishah, for revelation has not descended in the blanket of any one of you other than A'ishah - may Allah be pleased with her."
"21575","Ya'la ibn Mamlak from Umm Salamah. 977 - Hajjaj ibn Imran al-Sadusi narrated to us, Abu Salamah ibn Khalaf al-Jubari narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: My father informed me, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ya'la ibn Mamlak, he said: I asked Umm Salamah about the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and she said: He would pray Isha, then glorify Allah as long as Allah willed him to glorify, then sleep, then wake after a sleep like it, then sleep and rise - that would be his prayer until dawn."
"21576","Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah from Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her. 978 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Yahya, he said: I heard Ubayd Allah ibn Utbah narrating from Umm Salamah, she said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - was kept from the two rak'ahs before Asr, so he prayed them after Asr."
"21577","979 - Mahmud narrated to us, Tamim ibn al-Muntasir narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, from Sharik, from Talhah ibn Yahya, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would touch her while he was fasting."
"21578","Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from Umm Salamah. 980 - al-Khallal narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Umm Salamah: that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - when he wanted to sleep while in janabah would perform ablution as for prayer, and when he wanted to eat he would wash his hands then eat."
"21579","981 - al-Khallal narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salih and Usamah ibn Hafs narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Umm Salamah, that she said to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -: I have not performed the farewell circumambulation of the House. He said: When you pray, circumambulate behind the people upon your camel."
"21580","982 - Ishaq ibn Ahmad al-Khuza'i narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ala narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - commanded her to pray Fajr at Makkah."
"21581","Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ali from Umm Salamah. 983 - al-Khallal narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Hatim ibn Isma'il and Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, he said: Umm Salamah said: O Messenger of Allah, a woman whose husband has died - do you permit kohl? He said: One of you, when her husband died, would take a dung and throw it behind her back, then say: I will not apply kohl until this dung changes - but it is only four months and ten days."
"21582","Muhajir ibn al-Qibtiyyah from Umm Salamah. 984 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from Ubayd Allah ibn al-Qibtiyyah, he said: al-Harith ibn Abi Rabi'ah and Abdullah ibn Safwan entered upon Umm Salamah, and I was with them, and they asked her about the army that will be swallowed up - and that was at the time of Ibn al-Zubayr. She said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: One seeking refuge will seek refuge at the House, and Allah will send an expedition; when they are at a desert plain of the earth they will be swallowed up. She said: O Messenger of Allah, will one who was unwilling be swallowed up? He said: He will be swallowed up with them, but he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection upon his intention."
"21583","985 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Abu Yunus al-Bahili, from al-Muhajir al-Makki, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: An army will raid this House until, when they are at a desert plain of the earth, they will be swallowed up. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what about the coerced? He said: He will be raised upon his intention."
"21584","al-A'raj from Abu Salamah from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah from Umm Salamah. 986 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-A'raj, from Abu Salamah, he said: Zaynab bint Abi Salamah narrated to me, from her mother Umm Salamah, that a woman of Aslam called Subay'ah was under a man who died leaving her; Abu al-Sanabil ibn Ba'kak proposed to her and she refused to marry him. He said: It is not right for you to marry until you complete the longer of the two terms. She came to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and he said: Marry whomever you wish."
"21585","987 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, (ha). And Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, they said: al-Layth narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz, from Abu Salamah, that Zaynab bint Abi Salamah informed him, from her mother Umm Salamah, that a woman of Aslam called Subay'ah was under her husband who died leaving her while she was pregnant. Abu al-Sanabil ibn Ba'kak proposed to her and she refused to marry him. He said: It is not right to marry until you complete the longer of the two terms. She remained for twenty nights then gave birth, then came to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and he said: Marry. Fatimah bint Qays used to narrate from the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - when she was divorced irrevocably, that he commanded her to move to Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is blind - she lays aside her garments with him - before her waiting period ended. Muhammad ibn Usamah ibn Zayd used to narrate that whenever she mentioned anything of that, Usamah would throw at her what was in his hand."
"21586","Ali ibn al-Husayn from Zaynab. 988 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Muhammad and Abdullah ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Zaynab, from Umm Salamah: that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - ate from a sheep's shoulder, then the call to prayer was made, and he prayed Asr prayer without touching water."
"21587","Humayd ibn Nafi' from Zaynab. 989 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Humayd ibn Nafi', from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that a woman asked the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and said: O Messenger of Allah, I married off a daughter of mine, and measles afflicted her so her hair fell out, and we want to bring her to her husband. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Allah has cursed the woman who joins hair and the one who has it joined."
"21588","Abu al-Aswad from Urwah from Zaynab. 990 - al-Hasan ibn Ghulayb narrated to us, Imran ibn Harun al-Ramli narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, from Zaynab, from Umm Salamah, she said: Umm Sulaym came and said: O Messenger of Allah, is bathing obligatory upon a woman when she has a wet dream? He said: Yes, if she sees water, let her bathe."
"21589","Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah ibn Zam'ah from Zaynab from Umm Salamah. 991 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah ibn Zam'ah narrated to me, from his father, and from his mother Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, she said: It was my night in which the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - would come to me - the evening of the Day of Sacrifice - so he came to me. Wahb ibn Zam'ah entered upon me with another man of the family of Abu Umayyah, both wearing shirts. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Have you performed ifadah yet, O Abu Abdullah? He said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Take off your shirt. He took it off from his head, and his companion took his shirt off from his head. Then he said: Why, O Messenger of Allah? He said: This is a day in which you are permitted, when you have stoned the jamrah, to become lawful from everything forbidden to you except women. If you touch women before circumambulating this House, you become forbidden as you were before stoning the jamrah."
"21590","992 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah ibn Zam'ah, from his mother Zaynab, and from his father Abdullah, from Umm Salamah, she said: It was my night with the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and she mentioned similar to it."
"21591","993 - And from Ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr, from Yazid ibn Ruman, from Khalid, the freedman of al-Zubayr, from Zaynab, from Umm Salamah, similar to it."
"21592","Wahib from Zaynab. 994 - Abu al-Zinba' narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Wahib ibn Abdullah al-Ma'afiri, that he heard Zaynab bint Abi Salamah inform, from her mother Umm Salamah, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - observed i'tikaf the first year in the first ten days, then observed i'tikaf in the middle ten, then observed i'tikaf in the last ten, and said: I saw the Night of Decree in them but was made to forget it. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - continued to observe i'tikaf in them until the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - died."
"21593","Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Umm Salamah. 995 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Murrah, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his maternal aunt Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever drinks in vessels of gold and silver only drags fire of Hell in his belly."
"21594","Abdullah ibn Rafi' from Umm Salamah. 996 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Rafi', from Umm Salamah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - say upon this pulpit: I precede you at al-Kawthar. While I am upon it, you will be brought in groups, turned away from me, and I will call: Come here! Then a caller will call and say: They innovated after you. So I will say: Away with them."
"21595","997 - al-Hasan ibn Ghulayb narrated to us, Imran ibn Harun al-Ramli narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Abdullah ibn Rafi', from Umm Salamah, that while she was combing her hair, nothing startled her but the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - calling upon the pulpit, saying: O people, while I am at the Hawd, you will be brought group by group, and a party of you will go here and here. I will say: What is wrong with them - come to me! Then a crier will cry out and say: They changed after you. So I will say: Away, away."
"21596","998 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abdullah ibn Rafi', from Umm Salamah, that Umm Sulaym said: O Messenger of Allah, is bathing obligatory upon a woman who sees in her dream her husband having intercourse with her? He said: Yes, if she sees water. Umm Salamah said: O Messenger of Allah, can that be from a woman? He said: Yes - may your forehead be dusted - whence comes the resemblance to maternal uncles, with no mother for you? Whichever of the two fluids precedes to the womb dominates the resemblance."
"21597","999 - Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that Musa ibn Jubayr narrated to them, that Abdullah ibn Rafi' narrated to him, from Umm Salamah, she said: I know the most wealth that came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - before Allah took him: there came to him in the depth of night a pouch with eight hundred dirhams and a sheet. He sent it to me, and it was my night. Then he returned after the last Isha, prayed in the chamber at a prayer place of his - and I had prepared for him and myself, and I was waiting. He prolonged, then went out, then returned, and remained so until he was called for Fajr prayer. He prayed, then returned and said: Where is that pouch that tempted me last night? He called for it and distributed it, then said: Woe to you! I said: O Messenger of Allah, you did something you never used to do. He said: I would pray, then it would be brought to me, so I would leave until I looked at it, then return and pray."
"21598","1000 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Musa ibn Jubayr, from Abdullah ibn Rafi', from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - similar to it."
"21599","1001 - al-Hasan ibn Ghulayb narrated to us, Imran ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Abdullah ibn Rafi', from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saw camels, among some of which was a bell. When he heard its sound he said: What is this? A man said: The juljul. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: And what is the juljul? He said: The bell. He said: Yes - go and cut it off, then throw it away. He did so, then the man returned and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is wrong with it? The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell."
"21600","1002 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Abdullah ibn Rafi', from Umm Salamah, that two men of the Ansar entered upon the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - the hadith."
